551e9d18-f94f-4109-9c24-c7d5009ae902	2026-08-03 11:00:00.36362+00	dossier_v1	stub	\N	dev	3cde31fb-2569-467c-9632-1ecb6dc6c150	\N	{"answers": {"goal": "Lakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.", "schedule": "I run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.", "preferences": "Flat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.", "injuries_constraints": "Nothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six."}, "prefills": {"shoes": [{"id": "7dd93525-6b8a-448c-8a0c-9b6b03370cd0", "brand": "Brooks", "model": "Ghost 16", "isRetired": false}, {"id": "37f8a458-b459-49e4-9a40-9f598cfd0d89", "brand": "Saucony", "model": "Endorphin Speed 4", "isRetired": false}], "available": true, "defaultShoeId": "7dd93525-6b8a-448c-8a0c-9b6b03370cd0", "heartRateZones": {"zones": [{"maxBpm": 131, "minBpm": 112, "zoneNumber": 1}, {"maxBpm": 150, "minBpm": 131, "zoneNumber": 2}, {"maxBpm": 164, "minBpm": 150, "zoneNumber": 3}, {"maxBpm": 177, "minBpm": 164, "zoneNumber": 4}, {"maxBpm": 188, "minBpm": 177, "zoneNumber": 5}], "calculationMethod": "Custom"}, "recentTraining": [{"id": "0b98e572-ebd0-44b2-bca8-315dbf7c6978", "name": "Long run 11", "runType": "Long Run", "distanceM": 17382, "durationS": 6339, "startedAt": "2026-08-02T11:24:00Z"}, {"id": "af297822-66cb-4c5b-a473-2073c813e335", "name": "Easy 5", "runType": "Easy Run", "distanceM": 7828, "durationS": 2923, "startedAt": "2026-08-01T11:04:00Z"}, {"id": "4d217216-f14a-4332-85cc-a6a86dd0e16e", "name": "Easy 6", "runType": "Easy Run", "distanceM": 9413, "durationS": 3452, "startedAt": "2026-07-30T10:22:00Z"}, {"id": "83747e94-7bfe-493f-93d0-518390fc6b5f", "name": "Medium-long 6", "runType": "Easy Run", "distanceM": 9962, "durationS": 3605, "startedAt": "2026-07-29T10:09:00Z"}, {"id": "8fcc62f7-ea58-4f80-9629-7120000388fb", "name": "Easy 5", "runType": "Easy Run", "distanceM": 7815, "durationS": 2860, "startedAt": "2026-07-28T10:13:00Z"}], "unitPreference": "imperial"}}	{"summaryBullets":["Goal: Lakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.","Schedule: I run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and mor…","Constraints: Nothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.","Preferences: Flat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony E…","Easy heart rate zone about 131–150 bpm (from your running log)","Main shoe: Brooks Ghost 16"],"proposedBody":"# About you (v1)\\n\\n## Stance\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\n\\n## Goal\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\n\\n## Schedule\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\n\\n## Constraints\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\n\\n## Preferences\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\n\\n## From your running log\\n- Units: imperial\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\n\\n## Coaching notes\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one."}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	ok	\N	\N
022a035c-b5cf-4c82-a511-93fb06a749f9	2026-08-09 20:00:42.619014+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	3cde31fb-2569-467c-9632-1ecb6dc6c150	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W32\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W33\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-08-10\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-08-10, 2026-08-11, 2026-08-12, 2026-08-13, 2026-08-14, 2026-08-15, 2026-08-16\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":1,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W32 (Mon Aug 3 – Sun Aug 9, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 35.77 mi | 32.56 mi | 31.50 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 43m | 5h 19m | 5h 10m | +33m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 764 ft | 650 ft | 596 ft | +168 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 289 | 223 | 217 | +72 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 █████████████████████████████░░░░░░  81.9%   (4h 41m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  11.2%   (38m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.8%   (20m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **83.01%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 4 — Easy Run — 4.88 mi / 47m 33s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:44/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:46/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.1 → 143.1 (+5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.2% · Z2 96.8% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑75 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 5 — Easy Run — 6.94 mi / 1h 7m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.3 → 150.7 (+5.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 82.9% · Z3 17.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑190 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 47\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 6 — Tempo Run — 6.87 mi / 1h 2m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (79.8% max)  ·  Max HR 174  ·  Cad 351 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:54/mi / 9:46/mi / 7:50/mi / 7:52/mi / 7:45/mi / 9:59/mi / 9:57/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.2 → 139.7 (+3.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.4% · Z2 59% · Z3 6.4% · Z4 32.2% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑157 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 93\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 8 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 49m 9s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:51/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:52/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.1 (+5.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1% · Z2 99% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑154 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 9 — Long Run — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 82\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 9 — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:40/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:54/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi ▁▃▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.07 mi → 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (289) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (217) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.1 hrs (range 6.3–7.8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday, travelled for work.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Normal work week.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Fine. Legs a bit heavy on Thursday after the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Keen. The heat is the main thing, it was 25 degrees at 6 am by Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is 3:30 realistic for me from where I am now?\\\\n\\",\\"thread\\":[{\\"role\\":\\"coach\\",\\"body\\":\\"Here is what I understood from your answers, and from your running log where I could see it.\\\\n\\\\nSummary:\\\\n• Goal: Lakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n• Schedule: I run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and mor…\\\\n• Constraints: Nothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n• Preferences: Flat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony E…\\\\n• Easy heart rate zone about 131–150 bpm (from your running log)\\\\n• Main shoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nAccept to save it, or Reject to start over. The full text is under About you.\\",\\"createdAt\\":\\"2026-10-26T22:40:01.556Z\\"}],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W32\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-03T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-10T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"3cde31fb-2569-467c-9632-1ecb6dc6c150\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W33\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-10T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-17T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-08-10\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-08-16\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRepgutrDZkYEdy8t6sa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This week jumped about 10% to 35.77 miles, so next week should ease back or hold steady rather than push further. With the marathon 14 weeks out and easy pace sitting around 9:45 at a mid-Z2 heart rate, hitting 3:30 (8:00/mi) is a stretch from current fitness but achievable with a focused training block.\\n\\nI'm planning week 33 to hold around 33-34 miles with a quality session Thursday (hill strides or short tempo), an easy week structure Monday through Saturday, and a 13-mile long run Sunday finishing the last three miles at marathon pace, keeping heat in mind.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JkhLUpurtRrC9b9nXGTo3U","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nSolid week — 35.8 mi with 83% easy, long run stretched to 12 mi, and your tempo splits (7:45–7:52) show real fitness. We're 14 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week I want to consolidate rather than push the mileage dial again, start introducing marathon-pace feel on the long run, and respect the heat.\\n\\n## Concerns / flags\\n- **Relative effort jumped +33% over your 3-week average.** That's the kind of spike that, repeated, is how shin issues creep back in. One week like that is fine; two in a row isn't. So W33 holds mileage flat and keeps quality controlled.\\n- **Long-run drift was +7.4 bpm** (144 → 151) and you flagged 25°C at 6 a.m. That's heat tax, not a fitness problem — but it means pace targets on the long run should be by effort/HR, not the watch.\\n- **Thursday tempo structure was 3 fast miles sandwiched by easy.** Great session. Keep that template; we'll alternate hills and tempo weekly.\\n\\n## Your question — is 3:30 realistic?\\nHonest answer: it's a stretch but a reasonable one. 3:30 is 8:00/mi. Right now your easy pace is 9:45 at mid-Z2 and you ran 7:45–7:52 for 3 tempo miles — that's a fitness level that typically supports something in the 3:35–3:45 range today. You have 14 weeks, a sensible 5-day structure, and you're ramping carefully. If the next 6 weeks of base + strength work land cleanly and we see your long-run cruise pace drift under 9:20 at the same HR, 3:30 is on the table. If it doesn't, we aim 3:35 and run smart. We'll know by late September. Either way, the training looks the same for now.\\n\\n## This week — the \\"why\\"\\n- **Hold mileage ~34 mi** (slight pullback from 35.8) to absorb last week's load.\\n- **Thursday = hill reps** on your Thursday hilly route — strength without the systemic cost of another tempo so soon.\\n- **Sunday long run = 13 mi with last 3 at marathon-pace effort (~8:00–8:10/mi, cap HR at upper Z3).** First taste of goal-pace fatigue. If it's hot, run by effort and skip the MP miles — tell me after.\\n- Easy days properly easy: HR under 150, pace will take care of itself.\\n- Try to get both strength sessions in this week since you're not travelling.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W33","days":[{"date":"2026-08-10","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Walk/mobility if you want."},{"date":"2026-08-11","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"structure":"5 mi conversational, HR ≤150","paceOrHr":"~9:45–10:00/mi, Z2","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"Optional 20–30 min lower-body + core (calves, single-leg, hips)"},{"date":"2026-08-12","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"structure":"7 mi steady easy, finish with 4×20s strides on flat","paceOrHr":"Z2, strides relaxed-fast","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Strides wake up turnover without adding real load."},{"date":"2026-08-13","dayType":"quality","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":9656,"structure":"1.5 mi WU → 6×60s hill reps hard (easy jog down recovery) → 1.5 mi CD on hilly route","paceOrHr":"Reps by effort ~8/10; between in Z1","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4"},"notes":"Hills = strength + form, kinder to shins than another flat tempo so soon after last Thursday."},{"date":"2026-08-14","dayType":"rest","notes":"Work travel rest day."},{"date":"2026-08-15","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"structure":"5 mi easy on canal path","paceOrHr":"Z2, HR ≤150","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent knee), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges"},{"date":"2026-08-16","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":20921,"structure":"13 mi: first 10 easy (Z2), last 3 at marathon-pace effort ~8:00–8:10/mi (cap HR upper Z3 / ~164). If temp >22°C at start, run all 13 easy and tell me.","paceOrHr":"Easy 9:40–9:55; MP 8:00–8:10","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"First MP finish of the block — just a taste. Fuel: carbs + fluids beforehand, gel around mile 7."}]},"safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Heat on long runs","body":"You flagged 25°C at 6 a.m. last Sunday. Start earlier if you can, carry fluids, and if you feel dizzy, stop sweating, or get a headache that doesn't ease with water, stop and seek medical help. Running by effort/HR (not pace) in heat is the right call.","severity":"info"}],"settingsProposalBullets":["Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next","Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker","Revisit goal pace realism in late September"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6547,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2355,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":297}},"diagnostics":null}	200	42219	tool_use	6547	2355	0	0	ok	\N	297
562d2c1c-5489-41a5-aa68-71533b143cf2	2026-08-16 20:00:39.806972+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	08a10798-413e-497b-85cc-bb06f1c4a7bb	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W33\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W34\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-08-17\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-08-17, 2026-08-18, 2026-08-19, 2026-08-20, 2026-08-21, 2026-08-22, 2026-08-23\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":2,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W33)\\\\n\\\\n- Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next\\\\n- Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker\\\\n- Revisit goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W33 (Mon Aug 10 – Sun Aug 16, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 37.74 mi | 35.77 mi | 33.43 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 57m | 5h 43m | 5h 25m | +32m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 764 ft | 664 ft | +81 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 304 | 289 | 244 | +60 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.3%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  79.8%   (4h 46m)\\\\nZ3 █████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  13.3%   (48m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.3%   (19m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0.3%   (1m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.07%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 11 — Easy Run — 4.93 mi / 47m 57s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:44/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.5 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 12 — Easy Run — 7.92 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.3 → 149.5 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.2% · Z3 9.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 13 — Interval Run — 6.95 mi / 59m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:32/mi  ·  Avg HR 154 (81.9% max)  ·  Max HR 180  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:41/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:51/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.8 → 143.5 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.4% · Z2 40% · Z3 22.8% · Z4 32.1% · Z5 1.7%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑92 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 95\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 8/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 15 — Easy Run — 4.92 mi / 48m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:43/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 143.9 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 16 — Long Run — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑305 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 88\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 16 — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:38/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi ▁▁▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.9 hrs (range 6–7.6)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: All fine. Sunday was a slog in the humidity but nothing hurts.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. A bit worried the 800s were too fast early on.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I slow the long run down when it is this hot, or hold the pace?\\\\n\\",\\"thread\\":[],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W33\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-10T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-17T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"08a10798-413e-497b-85cc-bb06f1c4a7bb\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W32\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"3cde31fb-2569-467c-9632-1ecb6dc6c150\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W32 (Mon Aug 3 – Sun Aug 9, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 35.77 mi | 32.56 mi | 31.50 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 43m | 5h 19m | 5h 10m | +33m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 764 ft | 650 ft | 596 ft | +168 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 289 | 223 | 217 | +72 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░ 