mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.1 (+5.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1% · Z2 99% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑154 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 9 — Long Run — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 82\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 9 — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:40/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:54/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi ▁▃▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.07 mi → 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (289) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (217) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.1 hrs (range 6.3–7.8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday, travelled for work.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Normal work week.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Fine. Legs a bit heavy on Thursday after the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Keen. The heat is the main thing, it was 25 degrees at 6 am by Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is 3:30 realistic for me from where I am now?\\\\n\\"}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W34\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-17T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-24T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-08-23\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRetNeuXgZJR8gad5Cti","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since Thursday alternates between hills and tempo/MP, and last week was intervals with tempo the week before, this week should rotate to hills. I'll build mileage modestly from 37.7 up toward around 40.\\n\\nFor the plan: Tuesday easy 5mi, Wednesday easy 8mi, Thursday hills on a hilly route around 7mi with reps, Saturday easy 5-6mi, Sunday long run 14mi. On the questions — I'll recommend HR cap for slow long runs in heat, note the 800s pace was quick but acceptable given the RPE, and suggest revisiting the 3:30 goal realism in late September.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015LToGjwc4t4rNSUqKRP7Qm","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nStrong, controlled week — 37.7 mi, 81% in Z1+Z2, easy HR locked at 144, and your longest long run of the block (13.0 mi) came in even-split with no late pace fade despite the humidity. You're building the aerobic base cleanly. This week we'll push the long run to 14, swap Thursday to the hill route (per our Thursday rotation), and hold total volume around 40 mi.\\n\\n## Concerns / flags\\n- Thursday's 800s averaged 6:38/mi — that's faster than needed and you flagged it yourself. We'll address with hills this week (self-limiting effort), and when tempo/MP returns next week we'll put real pace targets on it.\\n- Long-run HR drift was +6.9 bpm with a Z3 tail (21% Z3). In this heat that's acceptable, but it's a signal to run long by HR, not pace.\\n- Sleep averaging 6.9 hr — fine, but keep an eye on it as volume climbs.\\n- No body complaints — good. Shin-splint history noted; we're ramping mileage ~5–8% per week, which is conservative.\\n\\n## Your questions\\n1. **Slow the long run in the heat?** Yes — cap by HR, not pace. Hold average HR ≤148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 8 even at honest easy effort, back the pace off 15–20 sec/mi. Pace will come back when the weather breaks; what we're protecting is aerobic quality and recovery for Tuesday.\\n2. **Were the 800s too fast?** A touch. 6:38 is roughly 5K pace — fine for RPE 8, but for marathon work we get more bang from slightly slower reps you can repeat week after week. We'll build that discipline when tempo returns next week. This week is hills, which naturally caps the top end.\\n3. **Is 3:30 realistic?** Too early to call. The honest marker is long-run cruise pace at HR 148 — right now that's ~9:40/mi; 3:30 needs ~8:00/mi marathon pace, so the gap closes with tempo/MP work this fall. We'll formally revisit in late September.\\n\\n## This week's plan — why\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's 13.\\n- **Wed easy 8**: mid-week aerobic anchor, keep in Z2.\\n- **Thu hills (hilly route)**: 6 × 60–75 sec uphill hard / jog down, inside a 7-mi run. Builds strength and leg stiffness without the pace trap you felt on the 800s.\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\n- **Sun long 14 by HR**: cap at 148 avg. If you want a small quality nudge, finish the last 2 mi \\"comfortably strong\\" (upper Z2 / low Z3) — only if HR allows.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W34","days":[{"date":"2026-08-17","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest."},{"date":"2026-08-18","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"structure":"5 mi conversational, Z2 (HR ≤150). Shake out Sunday's long run.","paceOrHr":"~9:45/mi, HR ≤150","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}},{"date":"2026-08-19","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":12875,"structure":"8 mi steady aerobic, keep in Z2. If HR climbs into Z3 by mile 6, ease pace.","paceOrHr":"~9:40/mi, HR ≤150","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}},{"date":"2026-08-20","dayType":"quality","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":11265,"structure":"Hill session on the Thursday hilly route. 1.5 mi easy warm-up, drills, then 6 × 60–75 sec UPHILL hard (strong, controlled — not a sprint) with easy jog-down recovery (~2 min). 1.5 mi cool-down. Target ~7 mi total. Effort self-regulated; don't chase pace.","paceOrHr":"Reps by effort (RPE 8), recoveries easy","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4"},"notes":"Rotation this week: hills. Next Thursday returns to tempo/MP."},{"date":"2026-08-21","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest."},{"date":"2026-08-22","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"structure":"5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only.","paceOrHr":"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}},{"date":"2026-08-23","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":22531,"structure":"14 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 before mile 8, back off 15–20 sec/mi. Optional: last 2 mi comfortably strong (upper Z2 / low Z3) only if HR allows. Fuel + fluids given the heat.","paceOrHr":"HR ≤148 avg; pace will fall where it falls","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Longest run of the block so far. Pace is the output, not the target."}]},"settingsProposalBullets":["Thursday rotation this week: hills (tempo/MP returns W35)","Long run governed by HR cap 148 while heat persists","Mileage target ~40 mi, +~6% on W33","Revisit 3:30 goal pace realism in late September"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9117,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2405,