41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 82\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 9 — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:40/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:54/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi ▁▃▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.07 mi → 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (289) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (217) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.1 hrs (range 6.3–7.8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday, travelled for work.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Normal work week.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Fine. Legs a bit heavy on Thursday after the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Keen. The heat is the main thing, it was 25 degrees at 6 am by Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is 3:30 realistic for me from where I am now?\\\\n\\"}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W35\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-24T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-31T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-08-30\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRewqiS3BzgG7m8scJZP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Given the mileage jump to 42.55 with high stress and poor sleep, I'm leaning toward pulling back slightly this week rather than pushing further—aiming for around 38-40 miles with Thursday's tempo/MP work and a long run of 13-14 easy miles.\\n\\nActually, after a big week like that, standard progression suggests trimming the long run to 12-13 to let it absorb properly, landing total mileage closer to 36-38. Laying out the week: rest Monday, easy 6 Tuesday, easy 7-8 Wednesday, tempo Thursday, rest Friday, easy 5 Saturday, long 13 Sunday.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UV2jLFoWF5uwGd1tVgZqC6","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nBig week — 42.5 mi, a 15-miler, and your Thursday tempo splits (7:39–7:47) are sharp. But sleep averaged 6.4 hrs, work stress was high, you missed a strength session, and Saturday's easy run \\"felt like work.\\" That's your body asking for a small step back, not another build. W35 is a light consolidation week: same 5-run shape, mileage trimmed to ~36 mi, Thursday rotates to tempo/MP as planned, and the long run pulls back to 13 with some marathon-pace feel at the end.\\n\\n## Concerns / flags\\n- **Load + life stress combo.** Relative effort has climbed three weeks running (217 → 272 → 342). On its own that's fine; stacked with 6.4 hr sleep and a work deadline it's the exact setup where shins start grumbling. Your W34 target was ~40 mi — you ran 42.5. We're pulling back a touch this week on purpose.\\n- **Long-run drift +7.3 bpm again.** That's heat tax more than fitness. Keep the HR 148 cap on the easy portion; the MP finish is by effort, not watch.\\n- **Saturday felt like work.** Not a red flag, just a cue. If next Saturday feels the same after an easier week, tell me.\\n\\n## Your question — handling travel weeks\\nSimple rules of thumb:\\n1. **Protect the long run and one quality session.** If you can only do 3 runs that week, make them Sunday long, Thursday quality, and one easy midweek.\\n2. **Drop easy miles first, not workouts.** The aerobic base is forgiving over 7–10 days.\\n3. **Cap the travel week around 70–75% of normal mileage** and treat the following Monday as a true rest, not a catch-up day. No doubling back to \\"make up\\" miles.\\n4. **If a hotel treadmill is all you have**, easy miles only — no quality on a strange treadmill.\\nSend me the dates of your next travel week when you know them and I'll pre-build around it.\\n\\n## This week — the \\"why\\"\\n- **Mileage ~36 mi (down from 42.5).** Deliberate absorption week after three straight builds.\\n- **Thursday = tempo/MP** per the rotation. 4 × 1 mi at MP (8:00/mi) with short float recoveries — introduces goal pace in bite-sized chunks before we extend it on long runs.\\n- **Sunday long = 13 mi**, last 2 at MP effort. Shorter than last Sunday on purpose; quality over distance this week.\\n- **Easy days properly easy** — HR under 150. If Tuesday still feels like a slog, cut it to 4 mi, no ego.\\n- **Both strength sessions** this week since you're not travelling. The one you skipped is the shin insurance.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W35","days":[{"date":"2026-08-24","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Sleep is the priority after last week."},{"date":"2026-08-25","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"~9:45/mi, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"5 mi conversational on the canal. If legs feel heavy, cut to 4 mi — no questions."},"strength":"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges"},{"date":"2026-08-26","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"Z2, HR ≤150","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"7 mi steady easy + 4×20s relaxed strides on flat at the end"},"notes":"Strides keep legs sharp without adding real load."},{"date":"2026-08-27","dayType":"quality","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"WU/CD Z2; MP reps 8:00/mi (upper Z3, HR ≤164); floats ~9:30/mi","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4","structure":"1.5 mi WU → 4×1 mi @ MP (8:00/mi) w/ 2 min easy float jog between → 1.5 mi CD. Flat loop."},"notes":"First real MP block of the build — goal is controlled, not fast. If first rep's HR is already Z4, back off to 8:10/mi."},{"date":"2026-08-28","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest."},{"date":"2026-08-29","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"Z2, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"4 mi very easy, pre long-run shakeout"},"strength":"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core — the shin insurance session"},{"date":"2026-08-30","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":20921,"paceOrHr":"Easy 9:40–9:55 (HR cap 148); last 2 mi @ MP 8:00–8:10/mi (HR ≤164)","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"13 mi: first 11 easy, last 2 at marathon-pace effort. If temp >22°C at start, run all 13 easy and tell me."},"notes":"Shorter than last week on purpose — this is an absorption long run with a small MP finish. Fuel: carbs + fluids beforehand, gel ~mile 6."}]},"safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Watch the stress + sleep combo","body":"Three weeks of rising training load stacked with 6.4 hr sleep and high work stress is a known setup for overuse niggles — especially given your shin history. The pullback this week is intentional. If anything shin-related starts whispering (soreness that lingers after warm-up, tenderness to touch along the bone), stop running and see a sports physio or your doctor before pushing on. Don't try to train through it.","severity":"caution"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13983,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2503,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":276}},"diagnostics":null}	200	42666	tool_use	13983	2503	0	0	ok	\N	276
8a3fc845-c7bd-40b4-8ebe-d08cb3573142	2026-08-30 20:00:41.936801+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	2b4f1b4a-62fe-4e58-912f-fc86a3098016	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W35\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W36\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-08-31\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-08-31, 2026-09-01, 2026-09-02, 2026-09-03, 2026-09-04, 2026-09-05, 2026-09-06\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":3,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W33)\\\\n\\\\n- Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next\\\\n- Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker\\\\n- Revisit goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Thursday rotation this week: hills (tempo/MP returns W35)\\\\n- Long run governed by HR cap 148 while heat persists\\\\n- Mileage target ~40 mi, +~6% on W33\\\\n- Revisit 3:30 goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W35 (Mon Aug 24 – Sun Aug 30, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 33.72 mi | 42.55 mi | 38.69 mi | -5.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 18m | 6h 44m | 6h 8m | -49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 587 ft | 988 ft | 832 ft | -245 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 271 | 342 | 312 | -41 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80%   (4h 15m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  15.9%   (51m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.7%   (9m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.45%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 25 — Easy Run — 5.04 mi / 48m 15s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 143.9 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑105 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelati