ft | 745 ft | 720 ft | +268 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 342 | 304 | 272 | +70 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.1%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.9%   (5h 27m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  11.2%   (45m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.8%   (28m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **82.01%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 18 — Easy Run — 6.17 mi / 59m 43s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139 → 144.2 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.7% · Z2 98.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 19 — Easy Run — 7.89 mi / 1h 15m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.6 → 149.5 (+3.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 96% · Z3 4% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑161 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 20 — Tempo Run — 8.14 mi / 1h 11m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 173  ·  Cad 352 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 7:47/mi / 7:39/mi / 7:45/mi / 7:42/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 140.3 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 53.3% · Z3 5.6% · Z4 38.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑223 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 22 — Easy Run — 5.18 mi / 50m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 345 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.2 → 143.9 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2% · Z2 98% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 36\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 23 — Long Run — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73.6% · Z3 26.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑420 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 103\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 23 — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:36/mi vs front 9:35/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.4 hrs (range 5.5–7.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Too tired Wednesday evening.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: High. Deadline at work, late nights Tuesday and Wednesday.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Tired more than sore. Saturday's easy run felt like work.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Hoping the next week eases off a bit.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nStrong, controlled week — 37.7 mi, 81% in Z1+Z2, easy HR locked at 144, and your longest long run of the block (13.0 mi) came in even-split with no late pace fade despite the humidity. You're building the aerobic base cleanly. This week we'll push the long run to 14, swap Thursday to the hill route (per our Thursday rotation), and hold total volume around 40 mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- Thursday's 800s averaged 6:38/mi — that's faster than needed and you flagged it yourself. We'll address with hills this week (self-limiting effort), and when tempo/MP returns next week we'll put real pace targets on it.\\\\n- Long-run HR drift was +6.9 bpm with a Z3 tail (21% Z3). In this heat that's acceptable, but it's a signal to run long by HR, not pace.\\\\n- Sleep averaging 6.9 hr — fine, but keep an eye on it as volume climbs.\\\\n- No body complaints — good. Shin-splint history noted; we're ramping mileage ~5–8% per week, which is conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n1. **Slow the long run in the heat?** Yes — cap by HR, not pace. Hold average HR ≤148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 8 even at honest easy effort, back the pace off 15–20 sec/mi. Pace will come back when the weather breaks; what we're protecting is aerobic quality and recovery for Tuesday.\\\\n2. **Were the 800s too fast?** A touch. 6:38 is roughly 5K pace — fine for RPE 8, but for marathon work we get more bang from slightly slower reps you can repeat week after week. We'll build that discipline when tempo returns next week. This week is hills, which naturally caps the top end.\\\\n3. **Is 3:30 realistic?** Too early to call. The honest marker is long-run cruise pace at HR 148 — right now that's ~9:40/mi; 3:30 needs ~8:00/mi marathon pace, so the gap closes with tempo/MP work this fall. We'll formally revisit in late September.\\\\n\\\\n## This week's plan — why\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's 13.\\\\n- **Wed easy 8**: mid-week aerobic anchor, keep in Z2.\\\\n- **Thu hills (hilly route)**: 6 × 60–75 sec uphill hard / jog down, inside a 7-mi run. Builds strength and leg stiffness without the pace trap you felt on the 800s.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\\\n- **Sun long 14 by HR**: cap at 148 avg. If you want a small quality nudge, finish the last 2 mi \\\\\\"comfortably strong\\\\\\" (upper Z2 / low Z3) — only if HR allows.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational, Z2 (HR ≤150). Shake out Sunday's long run.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-18\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady aerobic, keep in Z2. If HR climbs into Z3 by mile 6, ease pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-19\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Reps by effort (RPE 8), recoveries easy\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"Hill session on the Thursday hilly route. 1.5 mi easy warm-up, drills, then 6 × 60–75 sec UPHILL hard (strong, controlled — not a sprint) with easy jog-down recovery (~2 min). 1.5 mi cool-down. Target ~7 mi total. Effort self-regulated; don't chase pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\