 vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:54/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi ▁▃▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.07 mi → 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (289) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (217) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.1 hrs (range 6.3–7.8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday, travelled for work.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Normal work week.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Fine. Legs a bit heavy on Thursday after the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Keen. The heat is the main thing, it was 25 degrees at 6 am by Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is 3:30 realistic for me from where I am now?\\\\n\\"}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W36\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-31T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-07T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-08-31\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-09-06\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRf1XoWkeadaPStQdQ2n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is the week after a step-back week, so I'm building back toward ~40 miles with a long run of 15-16mi. I need to double-check the Thursday workout rotation since last week was intervals, so I'm trying to figure out whether hills or tempo comes next.\\n\\nSince the athlete handled the 800s well, I'll prescribe tempo/MP this week as marathon prep: easy 5 Tuesday, easy 7 Wednesday, tempo/MP 8mi Thursday, easy 5 Saturday, long 15-16mi Sunday, targeting ~40 miles total. Then I need to address the fueling question too.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BEHpVyTbYm1YVUujYyr1ni","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nClean step-back week — 33.7 mi, 81% easy, long run at 10.8 with no late fade, and you came out of it feeling the best you have in a month. That's exactly what a down week is supposed to do. We're 11 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week we build back up: ~40 mi, a proper marathon-pace workout on Thursday (per the Thursday rotation), and the long run stretches to 16.\\n\\n## Concerns / flags\\n- No body complaints, sleep bumped to 7.4 hr, stress down — all green lights to push forward.\\n- Thursday's 800s two weeks running have landed around 6:36–6:40/mi (5K effort). Fine as fitness proof, but for marathon work the money is in sustained tempo/MP volume. This week we swap in tempo — it will feel less flashy and more useful.\\n- Long-run drift was +8.5 bpm on Sunday with a Z3 tail (21% Z3). You held HR cap at 148 avg, which is what we asked. In this heat that drift is heat tax, not fitness. Keep running long by HR.\\n- Shin-splint history: 40 mi is the biggest week of the block. The ramp from 33.7 → ~40 is about +18%, which is bigger than I'd normally like. I'm comfortable because last week was a true step-back, you're well-recovered, and we don't exceed last block's peak of 42.5. If anything twinges early in the week, tell me and we trim Sunday.\\n\\n## Your question — fueling the long run\\nShort version: start fueling now, don't wait until the race to figure it out. Rough targets for runs ≥90 min:\\n\\n- **Before**: 40–60 g carbs 1–2 hr out (bagel + banana + honey, or oatmeal). 400–500 ml fluid.\\n- **During**: 30–60 g carbs per hour after the first 45 min — one gel every 30–35 min is the simplest pattern. Sip fluid every ~15 min; in this heat add electrolytes (tab in a handheld, or a sports drink).\\n- **Practice**: use the exact gels/drink you plan to use on race day. The gut trains like the legs do — the long run is where you build it. Expect some trial and error for the first 2–3 weeks.\\n- **After**: carbs + protein within ~30 min (even just chocolate milk works).\\n\\nFor Sunday's 16: aim for a gel at ~mile 5 and ~mile 10, plus fluids. If you've been going without, start conservative at 30 g/hr and work up.\\n\\n## This week — the \\"why\\"\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's long.\\n- **Wed easy 7 + strides**: aerobic anchor, strides to keep legs sharp before Thursday.\\n- **Thu tempo (8 mi total)**: 2 mi WU → 4 mi at MP effort (~8:00–8:15/mi, HR upper Z3 ≤164) → 2 mi CD. First real block of marathon-pace volume. If HR is pinned at Z4 to hold pace, back off — the HR is the governor, not the watch.\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\n- **Sun long 16 by HR**: cap avg HR ≤148. Pace will fall where it falls. If you want a nudge at the end, finish last 2 mi comfortably strong — only if HR allows.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W36","days":[{"date":"2026-08-31","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest."},{"date":"2026-09-01","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"~9:40/mi, HR ≤150","structure":"5 mi conversational Z2. Shake out Sunday's long run."}},{"date":"2026-09-02","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"Z2, HR ≤150","structure":"7 mi steady aerobic, finish with 4×20s relaxed-fast strides on flat."}},{"date":"2026-09-03","dayType":"quality","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":12875,"shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4","paceOrHr":"MP block ~8:00–8:15/mi, HR upper Z3 (≤164)","structure":"8 mi tempo: 2 mi easy WU → 4 mi continuous at marathon-pace effort (~8:00–8:15/mi, cap HR 164) → 2 mi easy CD. HR is the governor — if you need Z4 to hold pace, slow down."},"notes":"Rotation: tempo/MP this week. Hills return next Thursday."},{"date":"2026-09-04","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest."},{"date":"2026-09-05","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148","structure":"5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only."}},{"date":"2026-09-06","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":25750,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"HR ≤148 avg; pace is the output","structure":"16 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 before mile 10, back off 15–20 sec/mi. Optional: last 2 mi comfortably strong (upper Z2 / low Z3) only if HR allows. Practice fueling: gel at mile 5 and mile 10, fluids every ~15 min with electrolytes."},"notes":"Longest run of the block. Fueling is part of the session — see notes above."}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":18817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2479,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":388}},"diagnostics":null}	200	41537	tool_use	18817	2479	0	0	ok	\N	388
0b9f7eac-0c65-4ac6-9325-e804445884b6	2026-09-06 20:00:45.912204+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	5c020889-40bf-4ecb-8a67-3a92c6e840d3	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W36\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W37\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-07\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-09-07, 2026-09-08, 2026-09-09, 2026-09-10, 2026-09-11, 2026-09-12, 2026-09-13\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":3,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W33)\\\\n\\\\n- Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next\\\\n- Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker\\\\n- Revisit goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Thursday rotation this week: hills (tempo/MP returns W35)\\\\n- Long run governed by HR cap 148 while heat persists\\\\n- Mileage target ~40 mi, +~6% on W33\\\\n- Revisit 3:30 goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W36 (Mon Aug 31 – Sun Sep 6, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.41 mi | 33.72 mi | 38.00 mi | +6.4 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 49m | 5h 18m | 6h 0m | +49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 587 ft | 773 ft | +182 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 328 | 271 | 306 | +22 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  73.4%   (5h 1m)\\\\nZ3 ████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  22.6%   (1h 33m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.8%   (11m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **74.64%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 1 — Easy Run — 5.91 mi / 56m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:33/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:26/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑121 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 2 — Easy Run — 9.18 mi / 1h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 149 (79.3% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:25/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.3 → 151 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 80.9% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑180 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 60\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 3 — Marathon Pace Run — 8.22 mi / 1h 9m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:29/mi  ·  Avg HR 153 (81.4% max)  ·  Max HR 163  ·  Cad 356 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:35/mi / 9:31/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:56/mi / 7:56/mi / 8:01/mi / 8:01/mi / 8:01/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 141.8 → 148.9 (+7.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.6% · Z2 28.1% · Z3 68.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 90\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 5 — Easy Run — 5.00 mi / 48m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:41/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.8 → 143.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑118 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 6 — Long Run — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149 (79.3% max)  ·  Max HR 168  ·  Cad 346 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm) ⚠ above target (targ