\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 6 — Tempo Run — 6.87 mi / 1h 2m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (79.8% max)  ·  Max HR 174  ·  Cad 351 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:54/mi / 9:46/mi / 7:50/mi / 7:52/mi / 7:45/mi / 9:59/mi / 9:57/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.2 → 139.7 (+3.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.4% · Z2 59% · Z3 6.4% · Z4 32.2% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑157 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 93\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 8 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 49m 9s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:51/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:52/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.1 (+5.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1% · Z2 99% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑154 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 9 — Long Run — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 82\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 9 — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:40/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:54/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi ▁▃▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.07 mi → 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (289) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (217) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.1 hrs (range 6.3–7.8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday, travelled for work.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Normal work week.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Fine. Legs a bit heavy on Thursday after the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Keen. The heat is the main thing, it was 25 degrees at 6 am by Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is 3:30 realistic for me from where I am now?\\\\n\\"}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-07T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-14T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-09-07\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-09-13\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRf55zcM6VFG1sxEpLAF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Week 36 was strong at 44.4 miles with a confident 16-mile long run ending at marathon pace, and with 10 weeks left until the November 15 race I need to keep building without overreaching after jumping 6.4 miles from the prior average—so I'm thinking about whether to consolidate this week or build slightly, and trying to figure out where this week falls in the Thursday workout rotation given what the last couple weeks included.\\n\\nConfirming the rotation puts this Thursday on hills, I'm noting the long run heart rate drifted well above target last time, which means I should cap effort on the long run even as I nudge mileage up to around 17 miles with some marathon-pace work mixed in. I'm sketching the week: easy runs Tuesday and Wednesday, hill repeats Thursday, an easy Saturday, and the long run Sunday with a marathon-pace segment, landing around 42 miles total, plus starting to practice race-day gels now.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MP7H4hyTiPthGKE2bdzS8B","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nThat was a breakthrough week — 44.4 mi, a 16-miler with a genuine MP finish (7:58, 7:55 at the end of a long run), and you came out of it confident. We're 10 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week I want to keep the shape but not stack another mileage jump on top of last week's +6.4. We hold ~42 mi, Thursday rotates back to hills (per the rotation), and Sunday is 17 by HR with a shorter MP touch at the end. First real test of fueling, too.\\n\\n## Concerns / flags\\n- **Long-run HR drift was +13.4 bpm** on Sunday (143.5 → 156.9, with Z4 time in the MP finish). Above our ≤10 bpm target. Some of that is the MP close, some is accumulated load from a big week. We'll govern the easy portion by HR cap 148 again and keep the MP piece shorter this week.\\n- **Mileage jump last week was ~+6 mi** on the prior week. Another +6 this week would be the exact setup where your shins got cranky in your first block. Holding flat at ~42 mi is deliberate.\\n- **No body complaints beyond \\"heavy legs\\"** post-long — that's normal. Just want it noted so you flag anything sharper.\\n- Sleep 7.2 hr, strength 2/2 — all green.\\n\\n## Your question — gel on the long run?\\nYes. Now is the right time to start practicing. The rule for marathon day is \\"nothing new on race day,\\" which means we practice fueling in training for the next 8 weeks. Start simple:\\n- **One gel 10–15 min before you head out** (with water).\\n- **One gel at ~mile 6**, another at **~mile 11** on Sunday's 17.\\n- Wash each one down with a few sips of water — gels need fluid to absorb cleanly.\\n- Pick a brand you can get at the race expo or carry yourself. Try one brand this week, note how your stomach handles it, and we'll iterate.\\nTarget is ~30–60g carbs per hour on race day; two gels across a 17-miler gets you in the ballpark without overloading your gut while you're still learning.\\n\\n## This week — the \\"why\\"\\n- **Hold volume ~42 mi** to absorb last week's load before pushing again in W38.\\n- **Thursday = hills** per the rotation. 8 × 60–75 sec uphill. Builds strength and leg stiffness, kinder to the system than another MP block right after Sunday's finish.\\n- **Sunday long = 17 mi, HR-capped easy with last 3 at MP effort.** Shorter MP block than last Sunday (3 vs the extended Z3/Z4 segment that drove the drift). We're protecting the drift number while still touching goal pace.\\n- **Easy days properly easy** — Wednesday has been creeping into Z3; keep HR ≤150 even if that means slowing to 9:30+.\\n- **Both strength sessions** since you're home all week.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W37","days":[{"date":"2026-09-07","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Walk/mobility if you want."},{"date":"2026-09-08","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"structure":"5 mi conversational + 4×20s relaxed strides on flat at the end","paceOrHr":"~9:30/mi, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges","notes":"Shake out Sunday's 16. Strides keep turnover sharp."},{"date":"2026-09-09","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":12875,"structure":"8 mi steady aerobic on canal. If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 5, back off — don't chase the pace you had last Wednesday.","paceOrHr":"Z2, HR ≤150","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Mid-week aerobic anchor. Properly easy."},{"date":"2026-09-10","dayType":"quality","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":11265,"structure":"1.5 mi easy WU → drills → 8 × 60–75s UPHILL strong (not sprint) w/ easy jog-down recovery (~2 min) → 1.5 mi CD. ~7 mi total on the Thursday hilly route.","paceOrHr":"Reps by effort (RPE 8); recoveries easy Z1–Z2","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4"},"notes":"Hills this week per the Thursday rotation. Tempo/MP returns W38. Effort self-regulated — the hill caps the top end so you can't blow it up."},{"date":"2026-09-11","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest."},{"date":"2026-09-12","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"structure":"5 mi truly easy, pre-long shakeout","paceOrHr":"~9:40/mi, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core — the shin insurance session"},{"date":"2026-09-13","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":27359,"structure":"17 mi: first 14 easy at HR cap 148 (pace will be ~9:30–9:45). Last 3 mi at MP effort (8:00–8:10/mi, HR ≤164). If HR is already drifting hard by mile 10, drop the MP finish and just finish easy — tell me after.","paceOrHr":"Easy portion HR ≤148; MP close 8:00–8:10/mi, HR ≤164","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Fueling practice: gel 10–15 min pre-run, gel at mile 6, gel at mile 11. Water with each. Carry fluids given the distance."}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":23804,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2727,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":599}},"diagnostics":null}	200	45535	tool_use	23804	2727	0	0	ok	\N	599
54d5fe08-e87b-4a10-aff9-3864bf6b21f1	2026-09-13 20:00:57.160106+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	3c7734eb-98fd-4127-a3bb-52042324cf03	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W37\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W38\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-14\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-09-14, 2026-09-15, 2026-09-16, 2026-09-17, 2026-09-18, 2026-09-19, 2026-09-20\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":3,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W33)\\\\n\\\\n- Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next\\\\n- Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker\\\\n- Revisit goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Thursday rotation this week: hills (tempo/MP returns W35)\\\\n- Long run governed by HR cap 148 while heat persists\\\\n- Mileage target ~40 mi, +~6% on W33\\\\n- Revisit 3:30 goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W37 (Mon Sep 7 – Sun Sep 13, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 31.22 mi | 44.41 mi | 40.23 mi | -9.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 51m | 6h 49m | 6h 17m | -1h 26m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 955 ft | 843 ft | -98 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 225 | 328 | 314 | -89 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.5%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████████░░░░░  87.1%   (4h 14m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  9.3%   (27m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.1%   (6m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **88.64%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 8 — Easy Run — 6.03 mi / 56m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑167 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\