mi → 9:34/mi ▁▃▃█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi ▃▅█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8.1)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Deadline done.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Best I've felt in a month. Legs have some bounce again.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Ready to go again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. What should I be eating and drinking on the long runs? I've mostly gone without so far.\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBig week — 42.5 mi, a 15-miler, and your Thursday tempo splits (7:39–7:47) are sharp. But sleep averaged 6.4 hrs, work stress was high, you missed a strength session, and Saturday's easy run \\\\\\"felt like work.\\\\\\" That's your body asking for a small step back, not another build. W35 is a light consolidation week: same 5-run shape, mileage trimmed to ~36 mi, Thursday rotates to tempo/MP as planned, and the long run pulls back to 13 with some marathon-pace feel at the end.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Load + life stress combo.** Relative effort has climbed three weeks running (217 → 272 → 342). On its own that's fine; stacked with 6.4 hr sleep and a work deadline it's the exact setup where shins start grumbling. Your W34 target was ~40 mi — you ran 42.5. We're pulling back a touch this week on purpose.\\\\n- **Long-run drift +7.3 bpm again.** That's heat tax more than fitness. Keep the HR 148 cap on the easy portion; the MP finish is by effort, not watch.\\\\n- **Saturday felt like work.** Not a red flag, just a cue. If next Saturday feels the same after an easier week, tell me.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — handling travel weeks\\\\nSimple rules of thumb:\\\\n1. **Protect the long run and one quality session.** If you can only do 3 runs that week, make them Sunday long, Thursday quality, and one easy midweek.\\\\n2. **Drop easy miles first, not workouts.** The aerobic base is forgiving over 7–10 days.\\\\n3. **Cap the travel week around 70–75% of normal mileage** and treat the following Monday as a true rest, not a catch-up day. No doubling back to \\\\\\"make up\\\\\\" miles.\\\\n4. **If a hotel treadmill is all you have**, easy miles only — no quality on a strange treadmill.\\\\nSend me the dates of your next travel week when you know them and I'll pre-build around it.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mileage ~36 mi (down from 42.5).** Deliberate absorption week after three straight builds.\\\\n- **Thursday = tempo/MP** per the rotation. 4 × 1 mi at MP (8:00/mi) with short float recoveries — introduces goal pace in bite-sized chunks before we extend it on long runs.\\\\n- **Sunday long = 13 mi**, last 2 at MP effort. Shorter than last Sunday on purpose; quality over distance this week.\\\\n- **Easy days properly easy** — HR under 150. If Tuesday still feels like a slog, cut it to 4 mi, no ego.\\\\n- **Both strength sessions** this week since you're not travelling. The one you skipped is the shin insurance.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Sleep is the priority after last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on the canal. If legs feel heavy, cut to 4 mi — no questions.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-25\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy + 4×20s relaxed strides on flat at the end\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Strides keep legs sharp without adding real load.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"WU/CD Z2; MP reps 8:00/mi (upper Z3, HR ≤164); floats ~9:30/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"1.5 mi WU → 4×1 mi @ MP (8:00/mi) w/ 2 min easy float jog between → 1.5 mi CD. Flat loop.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First real MP block of the build — goal is controlled, not fast. If first rep's HR is already Z4, back off to 8:10/mi.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi very easy, pre long-run shakeout\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-29\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core — the shin insurance session\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy 9:40–9:55 (HR cap 148); last 2 mi @ MP 8:00–8:10/mi (HR ≤164)\\",\\"distanceM\\":20921,\\"structure\\":\\"13 mi: first 11 easy, last 2 at marathon-pace effort. If temp >22°C at start, run all 13 easy and tell me.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-30\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shorter than last week on purpose — this is an absorption long run with a small MP finish. Fuel: carbs + fluids beforehand, gel ~mile 6.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W35\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W34\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"df4fdcff-636a-435d-81f9-6d2bb269feb3\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W34 (Mon Aug 17 – Sun Aug 23, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 42.55 mi | 37.74 mi | 35.36 mi | +7.2 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 44m | 5h 57m | 5h 40m | +1h 4m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 988 ft | 745 ft | 720 ft | +268 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 342 | 304 | 272 | +70 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.1%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.9%   (5h 27m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  11.2%   (45m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.8%   (28m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **82.01%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 18 — Easy Run — 6.17 mi / 59m 43s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139 → 144.2 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.7% · Z2 98.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 19 — Easy Run — 7.89 mi / 1h 15m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.6 → 149.5 (+3.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 96% · Z3 4% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑161 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 20 — Tempo Run — 8.14 mi / 1h 11m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 173  ·  Cad 352 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 7:47/mi / 7:39/mi / 7:45/mi / 7:42/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 140.3 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 53.3% · Z3 5.6% · Z4 38.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑223 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 22 — Easy Run — 5.18 mi / 50m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 345 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.2 → 143.9 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2% · Z2 98% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 36\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 23 — Long Run — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73.6% · Z3 26.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑420 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 103\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 23 — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:36/mi vs front 9:35/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.4 hrs (range 5.5–7.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Too tired Wednesday evening.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: High. Deadline at work, late nights Tuesday and Wednesday.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Tired more than sore. Saturday's easy run felt like work.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Hoping the next week eases off a bit.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nStrong, controlled week — 37.7 mi, 81% in Z1+Z2, easy HR locked at 144, and your longest long run of the block (13.0 mi) came in even-split with no late pace fade despite the humidity. You're building the aerobic base cleanly. This week we'll push the long run to 14, swap Thursday to the hill route (per our Thursday rotation), and hold total volume around 40 mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- Thursday's 800s averaged 6:38/mi — that's faster than needed and you flagged it yourself. We'll address with hills this week (self-limiting effort), and when tempo/MP returns next week we'll put real pace targets on it.\\\\n- Long-run HR drift was +6.9 bpm with a Z3 tail (21% Z3). In this heat that's acceptable, but it's a signal to run long by HR, not pace.\\\\n- Sleep averaging 6.9 hr — fine, but keep an eye on it as volume climbs.\\\\n- No body complaints — good. Shin-splint history noted; we're ramping mileage ~5–8% per week, which is conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n1. **Slow the long run in the heat?** Yes — cap by HR, not pace. Hold average HR ≤148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 8 even at honest easy effort, back the pace off 15–20 sec/mi. Pace will come back when the weather breaks; what we're protecting is aerobic quality and recovery for Tuesday.\\\\n2. **Were the 800s too fast?** A touch. 6:38 is roughly 5K pace — fine for RPE 8, but for marathon work we get more bang from slightly slower reps you can repeat week after week. We'll build that discipline when tempo returns next week. This week is hills, which naturally caps the top end.\\\\n3. **Is 3:30 realistic?** Too early to call. The honest marker is long-run cruise pace at HR 148 — right now that's ~9:40/mi; 3:30 needs ~8:00/mi marathon pace, so the gap closes with tempo/MP work this fall. We'll formally revisit in late September.\\\\n\\\\n## This week's plan — why\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's 13.\\\\n- **Wed easy 8**: mid-week aerobic anchor, keep in Z2.\\\\n- **Thu hills (hilly route)**: 6 × 60–75 sec uphill hard / jog down, inside a 7-mi run. Builds strength and leg stiffness without the pace trap you felt on the 800s.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\\\n- **Sun long 14 by HR**: cap at 148 avg. If you want a small quality nudge, finish the last 2 mi \\\\\\"comfortably strong\\\\\\" (upper Z2 / low Z3) — only if HR allows.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational, Z2 (HR ≤150). Shake out Sunday's long run.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-18\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady aerobic, keep in Z2. If HR climbs into Z3 by mile 6, ease pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-19\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Reps by effort (RPE 8), recoveries easy\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"Hill session on the Thursday hilly route. 1.5 mi easy warm-up, drills, then 6 × 60–75 sec UPHILL hard (strong, controlled — not a sprint) with easy jog-down recovery (~2 min). 1.5 mi cool-down. Target ~7 mi total. Effort self-regulated; don't chase pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Rotation this week: hills. Next Thursday returns to tempo/MP.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-22\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤148 avg; pace will fall where it falls\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 before mile 8, back off 15–20 sec/mi. Optional: last 2 mi comfortably strong (upper Z2 / low Z3) only if HR allows. Fuel + fluids given the heat.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Longest run of the block so far. Pace is the output, not the target.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W34\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W33\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"08a10798-413e-497b-85cc-bb06f1c4a7bb\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W33 (Mon Aug 10 – Sun Aug 16, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 37.74 mi | 35.77 mi | 33.43 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 57m | 5h 43m | 5h 25m | +32m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 764 ft | 664 ft | +81 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 304 | 289 | 244 | +60 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.3%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  79.8%   (4h 46m)\\\\nZ3 █████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  13.3%   (48m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.3%   (19m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0.3%   (1m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.07%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 11 — Easy Run — 4.93 mi / 47m 57s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:44/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.5 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 12 — Easy Run — 7.92 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.3 → 149.5 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.2% · Z3 9.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 13 — Interval Run — 6.95 mi / 59m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:32/mi  ·  Avg HR 154 (81.9% max)  ·  Max HR 180  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:41/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:51/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.8 → 143.5 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.4% · Z2 40% · Z3 22.8% · Z4 32.1% · Z5 1.7%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑92 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 95\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 8/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 15 — Easy Run — 4.92 mi / 48m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:43/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 143.9 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 16 — Long Run — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑305 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 88\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 16 — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:38/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi ▁▁▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.9 hrs (range 6–7.6)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: All fine. Sunday was a slog in the humidity but nothing hurts.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. A bit worried the 800s were too fast early on.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I slow the long run down when it is this hot, or hold the pace?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nSolid week — 35.8 mi with 83% easy, long run stretched to 12 mi, and your tempo splits (7:45–7:52) show real fitness. We're 14 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week I want to consolidate rather than push the mileage dial again, start introducing marathon-pace feel on the long run, and respect the heat.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Relative effort jumped +33% over your 3-week average.** That's the kind of spike that, repeated, is how shin issues creep back in. One week like that is fine; two in a row isn't. So W33 holds mileage flat and keeps quality controlled.\\\\n- **Long-run drift was +7.4 bpm** (144 → 151) and you flagged 25°C at 6 a.m. That's heat tax, not a fitness problem — but it means pace targets on the long run should be by effort/HR, not the watch.\\\\n- **Thursday tempo structure was 3 fast miles sandwiched by easy.** Great session. Keep that template; we'll alternate hills and tempo weekly.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — is 3:30 realistic?\\\\nHonest answer: it's a stretch but a reasonable one. 3:30 is 8:00/mi. Right now your easy pace is 9:45 at mid-Z2 and you ran 7:45–7:52 for 3 tempo miles — that's a fitness level that typically supports something in the 3:35–3:45 range today. You have 14 weeks, a sensible 5-day structure, and you're ramping carefully. If the next 6 weeks of base + strength work land cleanly and we see your long-run cruise pace drift under 9:20 at the same HR, 3:30 is on the table. If it doesn't, we aim 3:35 and run smart. We'll know by late September. Either way, the training looks the same for now.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Hold mileage ~34 mi** (slight pullback from 35.8) to absorb last week's load.\\\\n- **Thursday = hill reps** on your Thursday hilly route — strength without the systemic cost of another tempo so soon.\\\\n- **Sunday long run = 13 mi with last 3 at marathon-pace effort (~8:00–8:10/mi, cap HR at upper Z3).** First taste of goal-pace fatigue. If it's hot, run by effort and skip the MP miles — tell me after.\\\\n- Easy days properly easy: HR under 150, pace will take care of itself.\\\\n- Try to get both strength sessions in this week since you're not travelling.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Walk/mobility if you want.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45–10:00/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational, HR ≤150\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-11\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional 20–30 min lower-body + core (calves, single-leg, hips)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, strides relaxed-fast\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy, finish with 4×20s strides on flat\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-12\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Strides wake up turnover without adding real load.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Reps by effort ~8/10; between in Z1\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"1.5 mi WU → 6×60s hill reps hard (easy jog down recovery) → 1.5 mi CD on hilly route\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Hills = strength + form, kinder to shins than another flat tempo so soon after last Thursday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Work travel rest day.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy on canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-15\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent knee), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy 9:40–9:55; MP 8:00–8:10\\",\\"distanceM\\":20921,\\"structure\\":\\"13 mi: first 10 easy (Z2), last 3 at marathon-pace effort ~8:00–8:10/mi (cap HR upper Z3 / ~164). If temp >22°C at start, run all 13 easy and tell me.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First MP finish of the block — just a taste. Fuel: carbs + fluids beforehand, gel around mile 7.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W33\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-14T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-21T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-09-20\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRf8zixdW5mMvqorVyjk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This Achilles pattern is concerning — pain during the tempo run, stiffness persisting into Saturday, then stiffness after Sunday's long run even without pain during it. That progression is a red flag telling me to recommend a conservative approach and professional evaluation rather than pushing through, so I'm thinking through how to structure week W38 (Sep 14-20) and answer whether the athlete should rest entirely or continue with easy running, plus how to help them judge whether something's seriously wrong.\\n\\nI'm laying out a scaled-back week: no tempo or quality work, Thursday's session replaced with rest or cross-training, and a Tuesday test run to gauge whether easy miles are even tolerable, with instructions to abort if pain exceeds a mild threshold or sharpens. The long run on Sunday stays flat and easy with no marathon pace work, total mileage dropping to roughly 20-25 miles, and I want to flag clearly that they should see a sports physio given the recurring pain and stiffness pattern, watching for red flags like swelling, limping, or worsening morning stiffness.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lt7ihcJjhMfKzgaNGFm7Py","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nWe're pulling the handbrake this week. Your right Achilles went from \\"tight\\" during Thursday's tempo (sharp enough to stop at mile 2 and walk home) to stiff on Saturday to stiff-after-sitting on Sunday. That pattern — stiffness that eases with movement but keeps showing up — is a classic Achilles warning sign, and the smart move 9 weeks out from Lakeshore is to back off *now*, get it looked at by a qualified sports physio or sports-med doc, and protect the block. One cautious week costs you nothing. A stubborn Achilles pushed through costs you the race.\\n\\n## Answers to your questions\\n**1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?**\\nShort answer: a few true easy days are okay *if* the Achilles passes a simple morning check — but no quality, no long run as planned, and we abort any run the moment it talks back. The specific test each morning:\\n- Can you walk down the stairs normally without a sharp pinch?\\n- Can you do 10 single-leg calf raises on the right side without sharp pain (dull \\"I feel it\\" is fine, sharp is not)?\\n- Is morning stiffness the same or less than the day before?\\n\\nIf yes to all three → short, flat, slow easy run is on. If no to any → that day becomes rest or a 30-min bike/pool session instead. No negotiating.\\n\\n**2. How do I know if this is serious?**\\nI'm a coach, not a clinician, so I can't diagnose this — and that's exactly why I want you to see a sports physio or sports-med doctor this week, ideally in the next couple of days. The signs that mean *stop running and get seen urgently*: sharp pain that makes you limp or change your gait, visible swelling or a lump on the tendon, a feeling of weakness pushing off, pain that wakes you at night, or anything that feels like a \\"pop.\\" Getting hands on it early is the single best thing you can do for your race.\\n\\n## What I'm changing this week\\n- **No tempo, no MP, no strides, no hills.** Quality is off the table until the Achilles is quiet and a professional has cleared you.\\n- **Long run is cut to 8 miles max, flat, by feel.** Not 17 (which is where the ramp was headed). We don't lose fitness in one easy week — we lose it over three injured weeks.\\n- **Mileage ~18–22 mi** (down from 31). All Brooks Ghost, no Endorphin Speed (carbon plate + aggressive geometry is not what a cranky Achilles wants right now).\\n- **Two optional cross-training swaps** (bike or pool) if the morning check fails.\\n- **Daily calf care**: gentle calf stretching (straight + bent knee) 2× day, and if your physio approves, slow eccentric heel drops are the gold-standard homework — but let them prescribe those, not me.\\n\\nThe goal this week is simple: finish Sunday with the Achilles quieter than Monday. If we get that, next week we start carefully reintroducing structure. If we don't, we extend the easy block another week. We will not do another real quality session until this is settled.\\n\\nSend me a quick note mid-week on how Tuesday and Wednesday feel, and tell me what the physio says.","safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Right Achilles — please get this evaluated this week","body":"The pattern you're describing — sharp pain mid-tempo that forced you to stop, stiffness the next morning, and stiffness after sitting on Sunday — is something a qualified sports physio or sports-medicine doctor should look at hands-on, ideally in the next few days. I can't diagnose it and I don't want to guess. Getting it assessed early is the single best thing you can do to protect the Lakeshore block.","severity":"caution"},{"title":"Red flags — stop running and seek care promptly","body":"Stop running and contact a clinician the same day if any of these appear: sharp pain that changes your gait or makes you limp, visible swelling or a lump along the tendon, weakness pushing off the right foot, a sudden 'pop' or snap, or pain that wakes you at night. Don't push through any of those to finish a run.","severity":"urgent"},{"title":"Daily go/no-go check before any run this week","body":"Each morning before running: (1) walk down stairs normally — no sharp pinch; (2) 10 single-leg calf raises on the right side without sharp pain; (3) morning stiffness the same or better than yesterday. If any check fails, that day becomes rest or 30 minutes of easy bike/pool instead of running. No ego runs this week.","severity":"info"}],"prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W38","days":[{"date":"2026-09-14","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day + full rest. Gentle calf stretching 2× (straight-knee and bent-knee, 30s × 3 each side). Book the physio/sports-med appointment today if you haven't."},{"date":"2026-09-15","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":4828,"paceOrHr":"~9:45–10:00/mi, HR ≤145","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"Only if the morning Achilles check passes. 3 mi very easy on the flat canal — no hills, no strides. Abort immediately if sharp pain or if you catch yourself favoring the leg. If check fails: 30 min easy stationary bike instead."},"notes":"This is a test run, not a training run. Finish feeling like you could have done more."},{"date":"2026-09-16","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"~9:45/mi, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"Only if morning check passes AND Tuesday ran clean. 4 mi flat and easy. Stop if the Achilles sharpens at any point."},"notes":"If Tuesday wasn't clean, swap to 30–40 min bike or pool run."},{"date":"2026-09-17","dayType":"rest","notes":"Deliberately rest today — this slot was tempo/MP in the old rotation. Not this week. Optional 30 min easy bike or pool run if you want aerobic time. No running."},{"date":"2026-09-18","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Keep up calf stretching."},{"date":"2026-09-19","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"4 mi flat and easy, pre-'long' shakeout. Morning check must pass. Abort on any sharp pain."}},{"date":"2026-09-20","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":12875,"paceOrHr":"By feel, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"UP TO 8 mi, flat, by feel. Not the planned 17. No MP, no strong finish, no hills. If the Achilles starts talking in the first 2 miles, turn around and come home — that's the right answer, not a failure. Fuel practice is still welcome (gel ~mile 4) since it costs the Achilles nothing."},"notes":"Goal of this run: finish with the Achilles no worse than it started. If physio says shorter, do shorter."}]},"settingsProposalBullets":["Pause Thursday hills/tempo rotation until Achilles is cleared by a clinician and symptom-free for 7+ days","Shelve Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 until Achilles symptoms resolve; daily miles in Brooks Ghost 16 only","Long run governed by symptoms this week — distance ceiling 8 mi, no MP finishes until further notice","Add a daily morning Achilles check (stairs / single-leg calf raise / stiffness trend) as the go/no-go for each run","Revisit the 3:30 goal after we have 2 clean weeks post-clearance — may need to adjust goal or race plan"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":25952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3355,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":529}},"diagnostics":null}	200	56777	tool_use	25952	3355	0	0	ok	\N	529
d9620f8f-090c-4d82-be08-f3953bd8f96a	2026-09-20 20:00:58.795634+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	785715c9-e1fa-4a05-a805-9fc07672efaa	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W38\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W39\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-21\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-09-21, 2026-09-22, 2026-09-23, 2026-09-24, 2026-09-25, 2026-09-26, 2026-09-27\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":4,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W33)\\\\n\\\\n- Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next\\\\n- Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker\\\\n- Revisit goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Thursday rotation this week: hills (tempo/MP returns W35)\\\\n- Long run governed by HR cap 148 while heat persists\\\\n- Mileage target ~40 mi, +~6% on W33\\\\n- Revisit 3:30 goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W38)\\\\n\\\\n- Pause Thursday hills/tempo rotation until Achilles is cleared by a clinician and symptom-free for 7+ days\\\\n- Shelve Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 until Achilles symptoms resolve; daily miles in Brooks Ghost 16 only\\\\n- Long run governed by symptoms this week — distance ceiling 8 mi, no MP finishes until further notice\\\\n- Add a daily morning Achilles check (stairs / single-leg calf raise / stiffness trend) as the go/no-go for each run\\\\n- Revisit the 3:30 goal after we have 2 clean weeks post-clearance — may need to adjust goal or race plan\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\