:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 7.6% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑397 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 105\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 6 — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149  ·  Drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:07/mi vs front 9:25/mi (faster than front half by 18s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi ▁▁▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi ▃▅▁█\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.2 hrs (range 6.5–7.9)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low to moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs a little heavy after the long run, otherwise good.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Confident. Marathon pace felt controlled for the first time.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is it worth trying a gel on the long run next week, or keep it simple?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nClean step-back week — 33.7 mi, 81% easy, long run at 10.8 with no late fade, and you came out of it feeling the best you have in a month. That's exactly what a down week is supposed to do. We're 11 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week we build back up: ~40 mi, a proper marathon-pace workout on Thursday (per the Thursday rotation), and the long run stretches to 16.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- No body complaints, sleep bumped to 7.4 hr, stress down — all green lights to push forward.\\\\n- Thursday's 800s two weeks running have landed around 6:36–6:40/mi (5K effort). Fine as fitness proof, but for marathon work the money is in sustained tempo/MP volume. This week we swap in tempo — it will feel less flashy and more useful.\\\\n- Long-run drift was +8.5 bpm on Sunday with a Z3 tail (21% Z3). You held HR cap at 148 avg, which is what we asked. In this heat that drift is heat tax, not fitness. Keep running long by HR.\\\\n- Shin-splint history: 40 mi is the biggest week of the block. The ramp from 33.7 → ~40 is about +18%, which is bigger than I'd normally like. I'm comfortable because last week was a true step-back, you're well-recovered, and we don't exceed last block's peak of 42.5. If anything twinges early in the week, tell me and we trim Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — fueling the long run\\\\nShort version: start fueling now, don't wait until the race to figure it out. Rough targets for runs ≥90 min:\\\\n\\\\n- **Before**: 40–60 g carbs 1–2 hr out (bagel + banana + honey, or oatmeal). 400–500 ml fluid.\\\\n- **During**: 30–60 g carbs per hour after the first 45 min — one gel every 30–35 min is the simplest pattern. Sip fluid every ~15 min; in this heat add electrolytes (tab in a handheld, or a sports drink).\\\\n- **Practice**: use the exact gels/drink you plan to use on race day. The gut trains like the legs do — the long run is where you build it. Expect some trial and error for the first 2–3 weeks.\\\\n- **After**: carbs + protein within ~30 min (even just chocolate milk works).\\\\n\\\\nFor Sunday's 16: aim for a gel at ~mile 5 and ~mile 10, plus fluids. If you've been going without, start conservative at 30 g/hr and work up.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's long.\\\\n- **Wed easy 7 + strides**: aerobic anchor, strides to keep legs sharp before Thursday.\\\\n- **Thu tempo (8 mi total)**: 2 mi WU → 4 mi at MP effort (~8:00–8:15/mi, HR upper Z3 ≤164) → 2 mi CD. First real block of marathon-pace volume. If HR is pinned at Z4 to hold pace, back off — the HR is the governor, not the watch.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\\\n- **Sun long 16 by HR**: cap avg HR ≤148. Pace will fall where it falls. If you want a nudge at the end, finish last 2 mi comfortably strong — only if HR allows.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-31\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational Z2. Shake out Sunday's long run.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-01\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady aerobic, finish with 4×20s relaxed-fast strides on flat.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-02\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP block ~8:00–8:15/mi, HR upper Z3 (≤164)\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi tempo: 2 mi easy WU → 4 mi continuous at marathon-pace effort (~8:00–8:15/mi, cap HR 164) → 2 mi easy CD. HR is the governor — if you need Z4 to hold pace, slow down.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-03\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Rotation: tempo/MP this week. Hills return next Thursday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-05\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\