· Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 73\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 30 — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:31/mi vs front 9:28/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi ▁▃▃█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi ▃▅█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8.1)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Deadline done.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Best I've felt in a month. Legs have some bounce again.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Ready to go again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. What should I be eating and drinking on the long runs? I've mostly gone without so far.\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBig week — 42.5 mi, a 15-miler, and your Thursday tempo splits (7:39–7:47) are sharp. But sleep averaged 6.4 hrs, work stress was high, you missed a strength session, and Saturday's easy run \\\\\\"felt like work.\\\\\\" That's your body asking for a small step back, not another build. W35 is a light consolidation week: same 5-run shape, mileage trimmed to ~36 mi, Thursday rotates to tempo/MP as planned, and the long run pulls back to 13 with some marathon-pace feel at the end.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Load + life stress combo.** Relative effort has climbed three weeks running (217 → 272 → 342). On its own that's fine; stacked with 6.4 hr sleep and a work deadline it's the exact setup where shins start grumbling. Your W34 target was ~40 mi — you ran 42.5. We're pulling back a touch this week on purpose.\\\\n- **Long-run drift +7.3 bpm again.** That's heat tax more than fitness. Keep the HR 148 cap on the easy portion; the MP finish is by effort, not watch.\\\\n- **Saturday felt like work.** Not a red flag, just a cue. If next Saturday feels the same after an easier week, tell me.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — handling travel weeks\\\\nSimple rules of thumb:\\\\n1. **Protect the long run and one quality session.** If you can only do 3 runs that week, make them Sunday long, Thursday quality, and one easy midweek.\\\\n2. **Drop easy miles first, not workouts.** The aerobic base is forgiving over 7–10 days.\\\\n3. **Cap the travel week around 70–75% of normal mileage** and treat the following Monday as a true rest, not a catch-up day. No doubling back to \\\\\\"make up\\\\\\" miles.\\\\n4. **If a hotel treadmill is all you have**, easy miles only — no quality on a strange treadmill.\\\\nSend me the dates of your next travel week when you know them and I'll pre-build around it.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mileage ~36 mi (down from 42.5).** Deliberate absorption week after three straight builds.\\\\n- **Thursday = tempo/MP** per the rotation. 4 × 1 mi at MP (8:00/mi) with short float recoveries — introduces goal pace in bite-sized chunks before we extend it on long runs.\\\\n- **Sunday long = 13 mi**, last 2 at MP effort. Shorter than last Sunday on purpose; quality over distance this week.\\\\n- **Easy days properly easy** — HR under 150. If Tuesday still feels like a slog, cut it to 4 mi, no ego.\\\\n- **Both strength sessions** this week since you're not travelling. The one you skipped is the shin insurance.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Sleep is the priority after last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on the canal. If legs feel heavy, cut to 4 mi — no questions.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-25\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy + 4×20s relaxed strides on flat at the end\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Strides keep legs sharp without adding real load.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"WU/CD Z2; MP reps 8:00/mi (upper Z3, HR ≤164); floats ~9:30/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"1.5 mi WU → 4×1 mi @ MP (8:00/mi) w/ 2 min easy float jog between → 1.5 mi CD. Flat loop.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First real MP block of the build — goal is controlled, not fast. If first rep's HR is already Z4, back off to 8:10/mi.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi very easy, pre long-run shakeout\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-29\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core — the shin insurance session\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy 9:40–9:55 (HR cap 148); last 2 mi @ MP 8:00–8:10/mi (HR ≤164)\\",\\"distanceM\\":20921,\\"structure\\":\\"13 mi: first 11 easy, last 2 at marathon-pace effort. If temp >22°C at start, run all 13 easy and tell me.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-30\\",\\"notes\\":\\