.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 96% · Z3 4% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑161 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 20 — Tempo Run — 8.14 mi / 1h 11m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 173  ·  Cad 352 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 7:47/mi / 7:39/mi / 7:45/mi / 7:42/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 140.3 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 53.3% · Z3 5.6% · Z4 38.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑223 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 22 — Easy Run — 5.18 mi / 50m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 345 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.2 → 143.9 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2% · Z2 98% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 36\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 23 — Long Run — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73.6% · Z3 26.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑420 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 103\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 23 — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:36/mi vs front 9:35/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.4 hrs (range 5.5–7.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Too tired Wednesday evening.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: High. Deadline at work, late nights Tuesday and Wednesday.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Tired more than sore. Saturday's easy run felt like work.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Hoping the next week eases off a bit.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nStrong, controlled week — 37.7 mi, 81% in Z1+Z2, easy HR locked at 144, and your longest long run of the block (13.0 mi) came in even-split with no late pace fade despite the humidity. You're building the aerobic base cleanly. This week we'll push the long run to 14, swap Thursday to the hill route (per our Thursday rotation), and hold total volume around 40 mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- Thursday's 800s averaged 6:38/mi — that's faster than needed and you flagged it yourself. We'll address with hills this week (self-limiting effort), and when tempo/MP returns next week we'll put real pace targets on it.\\\\n- Long-run HR drift was +6.9 bpm with a Z3 tail (21% Z3). In this heat that's acceptable, but it's a signal to run long by HR, not pace.\\\\n- Sleep averaging 6.9 hr — fine, but keep an eye on it as volume climbs.\\\\n- No body complaints — good. Shin-splint history noted; we're ramping mileage ~5–8% per week, which is conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n1. **Slow the long run in the heat?** Yes — cap by HR, not pace. Hold average HR ≤148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 8 even at honest easy effort, back the pace off 15–20 sec/mi. Pace will come back when the weather breaks; what we're protecting is aerobic quality and recovery for Tuesday.\\\\n2. **Were the 800s too fast?** A touch. 6:38 is roughly 5K pace — fine for RPE 8, but for marathon work we get more bang from slightly slower reps you can repeat week after week. We'll build that discipline when tempo returns next week. This week is hills, which naturally caps the top end.\\\\n3. **Is 3:30 realistic?** Too early to call. The honest marker is long-run cruise pace at HR 148 — right now that's ~9:40/mi; 3:30 needs ~8:00/mi marathon pace, so the gap closes with tempo/MP work this fall. We'll formally revisit in late September.\\\\n\\\\n## This week's plan — why\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's 13.\\\\n- **Wed easy 8**: mid-week aerobic anchor, keep in Z2.\\\\n- **Thu hills (hilly route)**: 6 × 60–75 sec uphill hard / jog down, inside a 7-mi run. Builds strength and leg stiffness without the pace trap you felt on the 800s.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\\\n- **Sun long 14 by HR**: cap at 148 avg. If you want a small quality nudge, finish the last 2 mi \\\\\\"comfortably strong\\\\\\" (upper Z2 / low Z3) — only if HR allows.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational, Z2 (HR ≤150). Shake out Sunday's long run.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-18\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady aerobic, keep in Z2. If HR climbs into Z3 by mile 6, ease pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-19\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Reps by effort (RPE 8), recoveries easy\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"Hill session on the Thursday hilly route. 1.5 mi easy warm-up, drills, then 6 × 60–75 sec UPHILL hard (strong, controlled — not a sprint) with easy jog-down recovery (~2 min). 1.5 mi cool-down. Target ~7 mi total. Effort self-regulated; don't chase pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Rotation this week: hills. Next Thursday returns to tempo/MP.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-22\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤148 avg; pace will fall where it falls\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 before mile 8, back off 15–20 sec/mi. Optional: last 2 mi comfortably strong (upper Z2 / low Z3) only if HR allows. Fuel + fluids given the heat.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Longest run of the block so far. Pace is the output, not the target.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W34\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W39\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-21T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-28T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-09-21\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-09-27\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRfDhTnd2ynMu6LyJvWf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm counting the symptom-free days against the 7-day clearance threshold—Tuesday had slight tightness early on, Wednesday showed a hint at the start, but Thursday's notes suggest things felt fine, so I need to pin down exactly when the clean streak actually began before hills/tempo can resume.\\n\\nGiven still no clinician clearance, I'll stay conservative: easy running only, building mileage from 26 to roughly 31-32, extending the long run slightly to 10 miles since things seem stable, keeping to the Ghost trainer only and avoiding hills until cleared. With the race 8 weeks out, I'm flagging that the 3:30 goal likely needs reassessment, and I want to keep urging a clinician visit while watching for any red flags.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LnSn3gZUmc9Qk3Ctxi9d5v","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nReally encouraging week. You held the easy-only guardrails, built back to 26 mi across 5 runs, and the Achilles went from \\"slight tightness first half mile\\" Tue → \\"a hint at the start\\" Wed → \\"fine on the flat\\" Thu → nothing Sat or Sun, no post-run stiffness. That's the trajectory we wanted. We're now 8 weeks out from Lakeshore (Nov 15). This week we build cautiously — still easy-only, Ghost 16 only, daily morning Achilles check as the go/no-go, and we nudge the long run from 8 to 10. No hills, no tempo, no MP touches yet.\\n\\n## Concerns / flags\\n- **Still no clinician check-in on record.** The W38 note was explicit: hills/tempo rotation stays paused until you've been cleared by a clinician AND been symptom-free for 7+ days. You've got a strong week of symptom-free running, but I don't want to add intensity on the back of self-clearance alone. See the callout — please get it looked at this week if you haven't.\\n- **Easy pace creeping down** (9:34 → 9:30 → 9:23 → 9:24/mi at HR 143–144). Good aerobic sign, but on a healing Achilles I'd rather you stay honest-easy and let pace be the output. Don't chase Wednesday's 9:15s.\\n- **Wednesday run drifted to Z3** (15.7% Z3, avg HR 148). Fine in isolation but it's the day easy becomes \\"steady.\\" Keep HR ≤148 this Wednesday.\\n- Sleep 7.5, strength 2/2, stress low — all green.\\n\\n## Your questions\\n**1. When can I do a hard session again?**\\nThe gate is unchanged: clinician clearance + 7 consecutive symptom-free days (no stiffness on morning stairs, no tightness in the first mile, nothing after the run). You've just completed what looks like your first clean week — so the earliest a quality session comes back is W40, and only if W39 is also clean AND you've got clearance. When we re-introduce, it'll be a soft return: a short strides-only session or a 2 × 1 mi at MP, not straight back into hills or a 4-mile tempo.\\n\\n**2. Does the missed week change what's realistic for race day?**\\nHonest answer: probably, yes. We're 8 weeks out and we've lost the Thursday quality rotation for ~3 weeks. 3:30 required MP work compounded over months — the fitness you built through W36 (that MP block at 7:58/mi) is still in the bank, but we need 4–5 clean MP sessions and 2–3 big long runs with MP finishes to sharpen it, and we don't have room for all of that now. My read: **3:35–3:38 is a realistic A-goal if the next two weeks are clean and quality returns in W40**, with 3:30 moved to a stretch \\"if the day is perfect\\" target. Let's make the call formally after W40 — I need to see one quality session back on the legs before I commit to a race plan.\\n\\n## This week — the \\"why\\"\\n- **~31 mi, all easy, Ghost 16 only.** +5 mi on last week is a sensible step; we're not rushing back to 40.\\n- **Thursday stays flat and easy** (not the hilly route). Hilly route returns only when quality returns.\\n- **Long run to 10 mi**, by HR, no MP finish. Within last week's ceiling philosophy but a modest extension because you had zero symptoms Sat/Sun.\\n- **Daily morning Achilles check stays in** as the go/no-go. If stairs or single-leg calf raise are stiff/painful, swap that day for rest and tell me.\\n- **Strength both sessions** — calf raises and slow heel drops are directly protective here.\\n- **Wednesday stays honest-easy** (HR ≤148, slow down if needed).","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W39","days":[{"date":"2026-09-21","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Morning Achilles check: stairs + single-leg calf raise. Note anything that isn't neutral."},{"date":"2026-09-22","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"~9:30/mi, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"5 mi conversational on the flat canal path. First mile deliberately slow — this is also the Achilles warm-up test. If anything beyond mild first-half-mile tightness, cut short and tell me."},"strength":"20–30 min: slow heel drops (straight + bent knee, 3×15 each side), single-leg calf raises, glute bridges, side plank","notes":"Go/no-go = morning Achilles check. Properly easy."},{"date":"2026-09-23","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":9656,"paceOrHr":"Z2, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"6 mi steady aerobic on the canal. Keep HR ≤148 — if it drifts into Z3 by mile 4, back off pace. Don't chase last Wednesday's splits."},"notes":"Mid-week aerobic anchor. HR is the governor."},{"date":"2026-09-24","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"~9:30/mi, HR ≤148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"5 mi easy on the FLAT canal — not the hilly route. No strides, no pickups. Just honest aerobic miles."},"notes":"Normally the quality day. Stays easy and flat until Achilles is cleared by a clinician and we've got 7+ fully clean days."},{"date":"2026-09-25","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest."},{"date":"2026-09-26","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":4828,"paceOrHr":"~9:40/mi, HR ≤145","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"3 mi truly easy pre-long shakeout. Short on purpose."},"strength":"20–30 min: heel drops, single-leg calf raises, core — the Achilles/shin insurance session","notes":"Short shakeout. If anything isn't right, swap for rest."},{"date":"2026-09-27","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":16093,"paceOrHr":"HR ≤148 avg; pace is the output","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"10 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148. No MP finish this week. If anything in the Achilles flares during the run — tightness that doesn't ease by mile 2, any sharpness, any limp — stop and walk home. Fuel: gel pre-run and one at mile 5, water throughout."},"notes":"Modest extension from last week's 8. The win is a clean run, not a fast one."}]},"safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Get the Achilles looked at before quality returns","body":"Last week was symptom-free and that's great news, but I want a qualified clinician (sports physio or sports med doc) to actually assess the Achilles before we put hills, tempo or marathon-pace work back on your plate. I can coach the running load; I can't evaluate the tendon. Please book that appointment this week if you haven't. Bring the W37 tempo-run notes with you.","severity":"caution"},{"title":"Stop signals during any run this week","body":"Walk home and message me if any of these show up: sharp pain in the Achilles, pain that makes you change your stride or limp, tightness that doesn't ease within the first mile, or swelling/warmth you can see or feel afterward. These are escalate-to-clinician signals, not push-through signals.","severity":"caution"}],"settingsProposalBullets":["Keep Thursday quality rotation paused through W39; earliest return is W40 and only with clinician clearance + 7 clean days","Keep Endorphin Speed 4 shelved; Ghost 16 only until quality returns","Formally revisit 3:30 goal after W40 — current working range 3:35–3:38 pending clean build","Keep daily morning Achilles check as the per-run go/no-go"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26431,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3449,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":535}},"diagnostics":null}	200	58331	tool_use	26431	3449	0	0	ok	\N	535
6bf9baad-2709-49d4-bb73-5922f0227b5b	2026-09-27 20:01:00.224227+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	a5660788-041e-4bad-b5fa-c3ee40b81b12	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W39\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W40\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-28\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-09-28, 2026-09-29, 2026-09-30, 2026-10-01, 2026-10-02, 2026-10-03, 2026-10-04\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":5,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W33)\\\\n\\\\n- Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next\\\\n- Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker\\\\n- Revisit goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Thursday rotation this week: hills (tempo/MP returns W35)\\\\n- Long run governed by HR cap 148 while heat persists\\\\n- Mileage target ~40 mi, +~6% on W33\\\\n- Revisit 3:30 goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W38)\\\\n\\\\n- Pause Thursday hills/tempo rotation until Achilles is cleared by a clinician and symptom-free for 7+ days\\\\n- Shelve Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 until Achilles symptoms resolve; daily miles in Brooks Ghost 16 only\\\\n- Long run governed by symptoms this week — distance ceiling 8 mi, no MP finishes until further notice\\\\n- Add a daily morning Achilles check (stairs / single-leg calf raise / stiffness trend) as the go/no-go for each run\\\\n- Revisit the 3:30 goal after we have 2 clean weeks post-clearance — may need to adjust goal or race plan\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W39)\\\\n\\\\n- Keep Thursday quality rotation paused through W39; earliest return is W40 and only with clinician clearance + 7 clean days\\\\n- Keep Endorphin Speed 4 shelved; Ghost 16 only until quality returns\\\\n- Formally revisit 3:30 goal after W40 — current working range 3:35–3:38 pending clean build\\\\n- Keep daily morning Achilles check as the per-run go/no-go\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.3%   (4h 17m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  12.1%   (39m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.4%   (21m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.51%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 22 — Easy Run — 5.16 mi / 48m 4s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.5 → 144.1 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 23 — Easy Run — 6.86 mi / 1h 3m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:07/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.1 → 150.3 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 86.4% · Z3 13.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑240 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 45\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 24 — Tempo Run — 7.01 mi / 1h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (79.8% max)  ·  Max HR 174  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:39/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 138.7 (+2.6 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.5% · Z2 57.5% · Z3 6.5% · Z4 33.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑121 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 92\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles no issue.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 26 — Easy Run — 3.85 mi / 36m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:18/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.4 → 143.2 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 97.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑30 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 25\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 27 — Long Run — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 76.1% · Z3 23.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑230 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 78\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 27 — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:12/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ +3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi ▁▅▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 143 → 144 ▁▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi █▃▁▃\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Nothing. I kept checking for the Achilles on the tempo and it was fine.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Relieved and ready to build again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is there anything I should keep doing for the Achilles through race day?\\\\n\\",\\"thread\\":[],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W39\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-21T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-28T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"a5660788-041e-4bad-b5fa-c3ee40b81b12\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"785715c9-e1fa-4a05-a805-9fc07672efaa\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 52\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. When can I do a hard session again?\\\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nWe're pulling the handbrake this week. Your right Achilles went from \\\\\\"tight\\\\\\" during Thursday's tempo (sharp enough to stop at mile 2 and walk home) to stiff on Saturday to stiff-after-sitting on Sunday. That pattern — stiffness that eases with movement but keeps showing up — is a classic Achilles warning sign, and the smart move 9 weeks out from Lakeshore is to back off *now*, get it looked at by a qualified sports physio or sports-med doc, and protect the block. One cautious week costs you nothing. A stubborn Achilles pushed through costs you the race.\\\\n\\\\n## Answers to your questions\\\\n**1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?**\\\\nShort answer: a few true easy days are okay *if* the Achilles passes a simple morning check — but no quality, no long run as planned, and we abort any run the moment it talks back. The specific test each morning:\\\\n- Can you walk down the stairs normally without a sharp pinch?\\\\n- Can you do 10 single-leg calf raises on the right side without sharp pain (dull \\\\\\"I feel it\\\\\\" is fine, sharp is not)?\\\\n- Is morning stiffness the same or less than the day before?\\\\n\\\\nIf yes to all three → short, flat, slow easy run is on. If no to any → that day becomes rest or a 30-min bike/pool session instead. No negotiating.\\\\n\\\\n**2. How do I know if this is serious?**\\\\nI'm a coach, not a clinician, so I can't diagnose this — and that's exactly why I want you to see a sports physio or sports-med doctor this week, ideally in the next couple of days. The signs that mean *stop running and get seen urgently*: sharp pain that makes you limp or change your gait, visible swelling or a lump on the tendon, a feeling of weakness pushing off, pain that wakes you at night, or anything that feels like a \\\\\\"pop.\\\\\\" Getting hands on it early is the single best thing you can do for your race.\\\\n\\\\n## What I'm changing this week\\\\n- **No tempo, no MP, no strides, no hills.** Quality is off the table until the Achilles is quiet and a professional has cleared you.\\\\n- **Long run is cut to 8 miles max, flat, by feel.** Not 17 (which is where the ramp was headed). We don't lose fitness in one easy week — we lose it over three injured weeks.\\\\n- **Mileage ~18–22 mi** (down from 31). All Brooks Ghost, no Endorphin Speed (carbon plate + aggressive geometry is not what a cranky Achilles wants right now).\\\\n- **Two optional cross-training swaps** (bike or pool) if the morning check fails.\\\\n- **Daily calf care**: gentle calf stretching (straight + bent knee) 2× day, and if your physio approves, slow eccentric heel drops are the gold-standard homework — but let them prescribe those, not me.\\\\n\\\\nThe goal this week is simple: finish Sunday with the Achilles quieter than Monday. If we get that, next week we start carefully reintroducing structure. If we don't, we extend the easy block another week. We will not do another real quality session until this is settled.\\\\n\\\\nSend me a quick note mid-week on how Tuesday and Wednesday feel, and tell me what the physio says.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day + full rest. Gentle calf stretching 2× (straight-knee and bent-knee, 30s × 3 each side). Book the physio/sports-med appointment today if you haven't.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45–10:00/mi, HR ≤145\\",\\"distanceM\\":4828,\\"structure\\":\\"Only if the morning Achilles check passes. 3 mi very easy on the flat canal — no hills, no strides. Abort immediately if sharp pain or if you catch yourself favoring the leg. If check fails: 30 min easy stationary bike instead.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This is a test run, not a training run. Finish feeling like you could have done more.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"Only if morning check passes AND Tuesday ran clean. 4 mi flat and easy. Stop if the Achilles sharpens at any point.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"If Tuesday wasn't clean, swap to 30–40 min bike or pool run.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Deliberately rest today — this slot was tempo/MP in the old rotation. Not this week. Optional 30 min easy bike or pool run if you want aerobic time. No running.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Keep up calf stretching.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi flat and easy, pre-'long' shakeout. Morning check must pass. Abort on any sharp pain.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-19\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"By feel, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"UP TO 8 mi, flat, by feel. Not the planned 17. No MP, no strong finish, no hills. If the Achilles starts talking in the first 2 miles, turn around and come home — that's the right answer, not a failure. Fuel practice is still welcome (gel ~mile 4) since it costs the Achilles nothing.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Goal of this run: finish with the Achilles no worse than it started. If physio says shorter, do shorter.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W38\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"3c7734eb-98fd-4127-a3bb-52042324cf03\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W37 (Mon Sep 7 – Sun Sep 13, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 31.22 mi | 44.41 mi | 40.23 mi | -9.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 51m | 6h 49m | 6h 17m | -1h 26m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 955 ft | 843 ft | -98 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 225 | 328 | 314 | -89 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.5%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████████░░░░░  87.1%   (4h 14m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  9.3%   (27m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.1%   (6m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **88.64%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 8 — Easy Run — 6.03 mi / 56m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑167 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 9 — Easy Run — 8.20 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.1 → 150.2 (+4.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.7% · Z3 9.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 10 — Tempo Run — 3.10 mi / 28m 1s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 145 (77.1% max)  ·  Max HR 177  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:36/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 133.5 → 169.4 (+35.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 7.1% · Z2 66% · Z3 5.4% · Z4 21.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑10 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Right Achilles tight from mile 2. Stopped at 3.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 3/10  ·  Pain: Right Achilles tight from about mile 2 of the session. Got sharper as I picked up the pace, so I stopped at 3 miles and walked home.\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 12 — Easy Run — 3.89 mi / 37m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:36/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 144 (+6.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.7% · Z2 97.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 5/10  ·  Pain: Achilles stiff for the first mile, eased after that. About a 3 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 13 — Long Run — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 79.7% · Z3 19.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 65\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: No pain while running. Stiff getting out of the car afterwards.\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 13 — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:16/mi vs front 9:18/mi (vs front half; Δ +2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi █▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7 hrs (range 6.2–7.7)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped the second one to rest the legs.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Worried about the Achilles.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Right Achilles, just above the heel. Tight and a bit tender to press. No swelling that I can see. It was fine until the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Anxious. I don't want to throw away the block over this.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\n2. How do I know if this is serious?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nThat was a breakthrough week — 44.4 mi, a 16-miler with a genuine MP finish (7:58, 7:55 at the end of a long run), and you came out of it confident. We're 10 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week I want to keep the shape but not stack another mileage jump on top of last week's +6.4. We hold ~42 mi, Thursday rotates back to hills (per the rotation), and Sunday is 17 by HR with a shorter MP touch at the end. First real test of fueling, too.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Long-run HR drift was +13.4 bpm** on Sunday (143.5 → 156.9, with Z4 time in the MP finish). Above our ≤10 bpm target. Some of that is the MP close, some is accumulated load from a big week. We'll govern the easy portion by HR cap 148 again and keep the MP piece shorter this week.\\\\n- **Mileage jump last week was ~+6 mi** on the prior week. Another +6 this week would be the exact setup where your shins got cranky in your first block. Holding flat at ~42 mi is deliberate.\\\\n- **No body complaints beyond \\\\\\"heavy legs\\\\\\"** post-long — that's normal. Just want it noted so you flag anything sharper.\\\\n- Sleep 7.2 hr, strength 2/2 — all green.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — gel on the long run?\\\\nYes. Now is the right time to start practicing. The rule for marathon day is \\\\\\"nothing new on race day,\\\\\\" which means we practice fueling in training for the next 8 weeks. Start simple:\\\\n- **One gel 10–15 min before you head out** (with water).\\\\n- **One gel at ~mile 6**, another at **~mile 11** on Sunday's 17.\\\\n- Wash each one down with a few sips of water — gels need fluid to absorb cleanly.\\\\n- Pick a brand you can get at the race expo or carry yourself. Try one brand this week, note how your stomach handles it, and we'll iterate.\\\\nTarget is ~30–60g carbs per hour on race day; two gels across a 17-miler gets you in the ballpark without overloading your gut while you're still learning.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Hold volume ~42 mi** to absorb last week's load before pushing again in W38.\\\\n- **Thursday = hills** per the rotation. 8 × 60–75 sec uphill. Builds strength and leg stiffness, kinder to the system than another MP block right after Sunday's finish.\\\\n- **Sunday long = 17 mi, HR-capped easy with last 3 at MP effort.** Shorter MP block than last Sunday (3 vs the extended Z3/Z4 segment that drove the drift). We're protecting the drift number while still touching goal pace.\\\\n- **Easy days properly easy** — Wednesday has been creeping into Z3; keep HR ≤150 even if that means slowing to 9:30+.\\\\n- **Both strength sessions** since you're home all week.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Walk/mobility if you want.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:30/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational + 4×20s relaxed strides on flat at the end\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake out Sunday's 16. Strides keep turnover sharp.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady aerobic on canal. If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 5, back off — don't chase the pace you had last Wednesday.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Mid-week aerobic anchor. Properly easy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Reps by effort (RPE 8); recoveries easy Z1–Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"1.5 mi easy WU → drills → 8 × 60–75s UPHILL strong (not sprint) w/ easy jog-down recovery (~2 min) → 1.5 mi CD. ~7 mi total on the Thursday hilly route.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Hills this week per the Thursday rotation. Tempo/MP returns W38. Effort self-regulated — the hill caps the top end so you can't blow it up.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi truly easy, pre-long shakeout\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-12\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core — the shin insurance session\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy portion HR ≤148; MP close 8:00–8:10/mi, HR ≤164\\",\\"distanceM\\":27359,\\"structure\\":\\"17 mi: first 14 easy at HR cap 148 (pace will be ~9:30–9:45). Last 3 mi at MP effort (8:00–8:10/mi, HR ≤164). If HR is already drifting hard by mile 10, drop the MP finish and just finish easy — tell me after.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fueling practice: gel 10–15 min pre-run, gel at mile 6, gel at mile 11. Water with each. Carry fluids given the distance.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W37\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W36\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"5c020889-40bf-4ecb-8a67-3a92c6e840d3\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W36 (Mon Aug 31 – Sun Sep 6, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.41 mi | 33.72 mi | 38.00 mi | +6.4 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 49m | 5h 18m | 6h 0m | +49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 587 ft | 773 ft | +182 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 328 | 271 | 306 | +22 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (