sy Run — 5.00 mi / 48m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:41/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.8 → 143.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑118 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 6 — Long Run — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149 (79.3% max)  ·  Max HR 168  ·  Cad 346 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 7.6% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑397 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 105\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 6 — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149  ·  Drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:07/mi vs front 9:25/mi (faster than front half by 18s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi ▁▁▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi ▃▅▁█\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.2 hrs (range 6.5–7.9)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low to moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs a little heavy after the long run, otherwise good.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Confident. Marathon pace felt controlled for the first time.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is it worth trying a gel on the long run next week, or keep it simple?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nClean step-back week — 33.7 mi, 81% easy, long run at 10.8 with no late fade, and you came out of it feeling the best you have in a month. That's exactly what a down week is supposed to do. We're 11 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week we build back up: ~40 mi, a proper marathon-pace workout on Thursday (per the Thursday rotation), and the long run stretches to 16.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- No body complaints, sleep bumped to 7.4 hr, stress down — all green lights to push forward.\\\\n- Thursday's 800s two weeks running have landed around 6:36–6:40/mi (5K effort). Fine as fitness proof, but for marathon work the money is in sustained tempo/MP volume. This week we swap in tempo — it will feel less flashy and more useful.\\\\n- Long-run drift was +8.5 bpm on Sunday with a Z3 tail (21% Z3). You held HR cap at 148 avg, which is what we asked. In this heat that drift is heat tax, not fitness. Keep running long by HR.\\\\n- Shin-splint history: 40 mi is the biggest week of the block. The ramp from 33.7 → ~40 is about +18%, which is bigger than I'd normally like. I'm comfortable because last week was a true step-back, you're well-recovered, and we don't exceed last block's peak of 42.5. If anything twinges early in the week, tell me and we trim Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — fueling the long run\\\\nShort version: start fueling now, don't wait until the race to figure it out. Rough targets for runs ≥90 min:\\\\n\\\\n- **Before**: 40–60 g carbs 1–2 hr out (bagel + banana + honey, or oatmeal). 400–500 ml fluid.\\\\n- **During**: 30–60 g carbs per hour after the first 45 min — one gel every 30–35 min is the simplest pattern. Sip fluid every ~15 min; in this heat add electrolytes (tab in a handheld, or a sports drink).\\\\n- **Practice**: use the exact gels/drink you plan to use on race day. The gut trains like the legs do — the long run is where you build it. Expect some trial and error for the first 2–3 weeks.\\\\n- **After**: carbs + protein within ~30 min (even just chocolate milk works).\\\\n\\\\nFor Sunday's 16: aim for a gel at ~mile 5 and ~mile 10, plus fluids. If you've been going without, start conservative at 30 g/hr and work up.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's long.\\\\n- **Wed easy 7 + strides**: aerobic anchor, strides to keep legs sharp before Thursday.\\\\n- **Thu tempo (8 mi total)**: 2 mi WU → 4 mi at MP effort (~8:00–8:15/mi, HR upper Z3 ≤164) → 2 mi CD. First real block of marathon-pace volume. If HR is pinned at Z4 to hold pace, back off — the HR is the governor, not the watch.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\\\n- **Sun long 16 by HR**: cap avg HR ≤148. Pace will fall where it falls. If you want a nudge at the end, finish last 2 mi comfortably strong — only if HR allows.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-31\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational Z2. Shake out Sunday's long run.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-01\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady aerobic, finish with 4×20s relaxed-fast strides on flat.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-02\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP block ~8:00–8:15/mi, HR upper Z3 (≤164)\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi tempo: 2 mi easy WU → 4 mi continuous at marathon-pace effort (~8:00–8:15/mi, cap HR 164) → 2 mi easy CD. HR is the governor — if you need Z4 to hold pace, slow down.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-03\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Rotation: tempo/MP this week. Hills return next Thursday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-05\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤148 avg; pace is the output\\",\\"distanceM\\":25750,\\"structure\\":\\"16 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 before mile 10, back off 15–20 sec/mi. Optional: last 2 mi comfortably strong (upper Z2 / low Z3) only if HR allows. Practice fueling: gel at mile 5 and mile 10, fluids every ~15 min with electrolytes.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-06\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Longest run of the block. Fueling is part of the session — see notes above.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W36\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W35\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"2b4f1b4a-62fe-4e58-912f-fc86a3098016\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W35 (Mon Aug 24 – Sun Aug 30, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 33.72 mi | 42.55 mi | 38.69 mi | -5.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 18m | 6h 44m | 6h 8m | -49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 587 ft | 988 ft | 832 ft | -245 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 271 | 342 | 312 | -41 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80%   (4h 15m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  15.9%   (51m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.7%   (9m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.45%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 25 — Easy Run — 5.04 mi / 48m 15s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 143.9 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑105 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 26 — Easy Run — 6.92 mi / 1h 5m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:30/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.2 → 150 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 92.4% · Z3 7.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 46\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 27 — Interval Run — 5.99 mi / 52m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 153 (80.9% max)  ·  Max HR 176  ·  Cad 349 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:39/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:34/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 140.2 → 146.3 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.8% · Z2 35.7% · Z3 44.4% · Z4 16.1% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 85\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 29 — Easy Run — 4.90 mi / 47m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:39/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:36/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.4 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑79 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 30 — Long Run — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 73\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 30 — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:31/mi vs front 9:28/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi ▁▃▃█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi ▃▅█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8.1)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Deadline done.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Best I've felt in a month. Legs have some bounce again.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Ready to go again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. What should I be eating and drinking on the long runs? I've mostly gone without so far.\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBig week — 42.5 mi, a 15-miler, and your Thursday tempo splits (7:39–7:47) are sharp. But sleep averaged 6.4 hrs, work stress was high, you missed a strength session, and Saturday's easy run \\\\\\"felt like work.\\\\\\" That's your body asking for a small step back, not another build. W35 is a light consolidation week: same 5-run shape, mileage trimmed to ~36 mi, Thursday rotates to tempo/MP as planned, and the long run pulls back to 13 with some marathon-pace feel at the end.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Load + life stress combo.** Relative effort has climbed three weeks running (217 → 272 → 342). On its own that's fine; stacked with 6.4 hr sleep and a work deadline it's the exact setup where shins start grumbling. Your W34 target was ~40 mi — you ran 42.5. We're pulling back a touch this week on purpose.\\\\n- **Long-run drift +7.3 bpm again.** That's heat tax more than fitness. Keep the HR 148 cap on the easy portion; the MP finish is by effort, not watch.\\\\n- **Saturday felt like work.** Not a red flag, just a cue. If next Saturday feels the same after an easier week, tell me.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — handling travel weeks\\\\nSimple rules of thumb:\\\\n1. **Protect the long run and one quality session.** If you can only do 3 runs that week, make them Sunday long, Thursday quality, and one easy midweek.\\\\n2. **Drop easy miles first, not workouts.** The aerobic base is forgiving over 7–10 days.\\\\n3. **Cap the travel week around 70–75% of normal mileage** and treat the following Monday as a true rest, not a catch-up day. No doubling back to \\\\\\"make up\\\\\\" miles.\\\\n4. **If a hotel treadmill is all you have**, easy miles only — no quality on a strange treadmill.\\\\nSend me the dates of your next travel week when you know them and I'll pre-build around it.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mileage ~36 mi (down from 42.5).** Deliberate absorption week after three straight builds.\\\\n- **Thursday = tempo/MP** per the rotation. 4 × 1 mi at MP (8:00/mi) with short float recoveries — introduces goal pace in bite-sized chunks before we extend it on long runs.\\\\n- **Sunday long = 13 mi**, last 2 at MP effort. Shorter than last Sunday on purpose; quality over distance this week.\\\\n- **Easy days properly easy** — HR under 150. If Tuesday still feels like a slog, cut it to 4 mi, no ego.\\\\n- **Both strength sessions** this week since you're not travelling. The one you skipped is the shin insurance.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Sleep is the priority after last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on the canal. If legs feel heavy, cut to 4 mi — no questions.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-25\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy + 4×20s relaxed strides on flat at the end\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Strides keep legs sharp without adding real load.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"WU/CD Z2; MP reps 8:00/mi (upper Z3, HR ≤164); floats ~9:30/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"1.5 mi WU → 4×1 mi @ MP (8:00/mi) w/ 2 min easy float jog between → 1.5 mi CD. Flat loop.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First real MP block of the build — goal is controlled, not fast. If first rep's HR is already Z4, back off to 8:10/mi.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi very easy, pre long-run shakeout\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-29\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core — the shin insurance session\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy 9:40–9:55 (HR cap 148); last 2 mi @ MP 8:00–8:10/mi (HR ≤164)\\",\\"distanceM\\":20921,\\"structure\\":\\"13 mi: first 11 easy, last 2 at marathon-pace effort. If temp >22°C at start, run all 13 easy and tell me.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-30\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shorter than last week on purpose — this is an absorption long run with a small MP finish. Fuel: carbs + fluids beforehand, gel ~mile 6.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W35\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W40\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-28T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-05T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-09-28\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-10-04\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRfV1uhm2zU4bjUvm9h5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting — the athlete jumped the gun and ran the tempo early despite the pause being officially through W39, but reported no Achilles issues. W40 becomes the earliest allowed return, though I still don't know if clinician clearance actually happened, which matters for whether this counts as compliant.\\n\\nWith the marathon Nov 15, that's roughly 6-7 weeks out, so I'm building a cautious reintroduction: ~37-40 mi week, modest Thursday tempo or hills, Sunday long run around 14-15 mi, and keeping the daily morning Achilles check non-negotiable through race day. I'm leaning toward repeating the tempo/MP format Thursday rather than hills since it seemed to go well and is likely gentler on the Achilles than hill work, then laying out the week day-by-day with easy runs, a travel rest day, and a long run Sunday.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V4u9vH9w5oY9JyP7fBcfkT","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nWelcome back to a real training week. The Achilles sat quiet through a 35-mile week that included a tempo Thursday, and Sunday's 12 at HR 148 looked clean (back half a touch faster than the front — exactly what we want). With Lakeshore seven weeks out, W40 is where we rebuild structure: modest mileage bump to ~39 mi, a controlled MP tempo on Thursday, and a long run back out to 14 with a short goal-pace touch at the end.\\n\\nOne honest note: last Thursday's tempo technically beat the plan — the quality rotation was supposed to wait on clinician clearance plus 7 clean days. It went fine and the Achilles didn't flinch, which is good news. From here, please keep me posted on whether you've actually seen a physio/sports-med doc. If you have and they're happy, we're green. If you haven't, I'd still love you to book one as insurance, because we're going to progressively ask more of that tendon over the next month.\\n\\n## Concerns / flags\\n- **Achilles history is still recent.** Keep the morning check every day — stairs down, 10 single-leg calf raises, stiffness trend. Sharp pinch or worsening stiffness = that day's run becomes rest or a bike spin, no debate.\\n- **Sunday's drift was +8.8 bpm** over 12 mi — within our ≤10 target but close. Heat may still be in play. Long run stays HR-governed this week.\\n- **Mileage ramp:** 26 → 35 → 39 is a reasonable progression, not aggressive. We don't exceed last block's peak this week.\\n- **Shoe reintroduction:** Endorphin Speed 4 can come back for Thursday's workout only, since last week's session was clean. Daily miles stay in the Ghost.\\n- **3:30 goal:** still working range 3:35–3:38 per the W39 note. Let's see this week and next, then I'll call it. Thursday's MP work this week is at 8:05/mi (≈3:32 pace) — if that feels controlled, we're in business.\\n\\n## Your question — Achilles care through race day\\nYes, this is now part of the plan from here to Nov 15. Three things, non-negotiable:\\n\\n1. **Daily morning check** — the same stairs / single-leg calf raise / stiffness scan. 30 seconds. Any sharp pain or worsening stiffness = that day is rest or cross-train. Tell me in the next check-in if it flares.\\n2. **Calf strength 2× per week** — straight-knee and bent-knee heel raises (3×12 each side), ideally slow eccentric lowers. If your physio has given you a specific heel-drop protocol, do theirs over mine.\\n3. **Warm up properly for quality days** — never jump straight into fast running. The 1.5–2 mi easy warm-up on workout days is the Achilles's friend. On race morning: 10 min easy walk-jog + a few relaxed strides before the gun.\\n\\nAlso: no spikes, no track flats, and keep the Endorphin Speed for workouts only — not daily miles. If anything changes, we adjust — this isn't fire-and-forget.\\n\\n## This week — the \\"why\\"\\n- **Tue easy 6 + strides**: shake out Sunday's long, strides reintroduce turnover before Thursday.\\n- **Wed easy 7**: aerobic anchor, keep HR ≤150 even if it means 9:30+ pace.\\n- **Thu MP tempo (7.5 mi total)**: 1.5 WU → 4 mi @ MP (8:05/mi, HR ≤164) → 2 CD. Builds goal-pace volume in a controlled block. This is kinder to the Achilles than hill reps right now, so we hold hills off one more week.\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\n- **Sun long 14**: first 12 easy by HR cap 148, last 2 at MP effort if HR allows. Shorter MP touch than peak training — we're rebuilding the long run, not peaking it yet.\\n- **Strength 2×** — the calf/single-leg session is the Achilles insurance.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W40","days":[{"date":"2026-09-28","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Morning Achilles check. Calf stretching 2× (straight + bent knee, 30s × 3 each side)."},{"date":"2026-09-29","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":9656,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"~9:20/mi, HR ≤148","structure":"6 mi conversational on the flat canal + 4×20s relaxed strides at the end on flat ground. Strides should feel smooth, not sprinty."},"strength":"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent, 3×12 slow eccentric), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges — the Achilles insurance session","notes":"Morning check first. If anything sharp, swap to 30 min easy bike and text me."},{"date":"2026-09-30","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"Z2, HR ≤150","structure":"7 mi steady aerobic on canal. If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 5, back off — pace is the output, HR is the governor."}},{"date":"2026-10-01","dayType":"quality","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":12070,"shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4","paceOrHr":"WU/CD Z2; MP block 8:05/mi, HR ≤164","structure":"7.5 mi MP tempo: 1.5 mi easy WU + drills → 4 mi continuous at marathon-pace effort (8:05/mi, cap HR 164) → 2 mi easy CD. Flat canal — no hills on this one."},"notes":"First real MP block since the Achilles scare. If anything sharpens in the WU, abort and come home easy — this is a test session as much as a training session. Hills return in W41 if this week is clean."},{"date":"2026-10-02","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Keep up calf stretching."},{"date":"2026-10-03","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"~9:40/mi, HR ≤148","structure":"5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only."},"strength":"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core"},{"date":"2026-10-04","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":22531,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"Easy portion HR ≤148 (pace will be ~9:20–9:35); optional last 2 mi @ MP 8:05/mi, HR ≤164","structure":"14 mi: first 12 easy by HR cap 148. Last 2 mi at marathon-pace effort IF HR has stayed under cap and the Achilles is quiet. If HR is drifting hard by mile 9, drop the MP finish and jog it in — tell me after."},"notes":"Fueling practice: gel 10–15 min pre-run, gel at mile 5, gel at mile 10. Water with each. This is a rebuild long run, not a peak — bank the clean execution."}]},"safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Keep the Achilles plan active","body":"Last week was clean, which is great — but the tendon is still in the \\"earning trust\\" phase. Keep the morning check (stairs down, 10 single-leg calf raises, stiffness scan) every day as the per-run go/no-go. Any sharp pain, visible swelling, a lump on the tendon, weakness pushing off, a \\"pop,\\" or pain that wakes you at night — stop running and get seen by a sports physio or sports-medicine doctor. I'm your coach, not a clinician, so I can't diagnose or treat this; please loop in a professional if symptoms return.","severity":"caution"},{"title":"Confirm clinician clearance","body":"The plan called for clinician sign-off before quality returned. If you've seen a sports physio or sports-med doc and they're happy, we're on track. If you haven't yet, please book a visit this week as insurance — we're going to progressively load that tendon over the next month and I'd rather have eyes on it now than react later.","severity":"info"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26633,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3646,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":668}},"diagnostics":null}	200	59832	tool_use	26633	3646	0	0	ok	\N	668
c461eb7f-5d8d-45b8-9dcf-fcdc48f1781e	2026-10-04 20:01:53.680403+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	926df228-422a-4204-bf31-375758fd30e6	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W40\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W41\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-10-05\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-10-05, 2026-10-06, 2026-10-07, 2026-10-08, 2026-10-09, 2026-10-10, 2026-10-11\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":5,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W33)\\\\n\\\\n- Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next\\\\n- Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker\\\\n- Revisit goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Thursday rotation this week: hills (tempo/MP returns W35)\\\\n- Long run governed by HR cap 148 while heat persists\\\\n- Mileage target ~40 mi, +~6% on W33\\\\n- Revisit 3:30 goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W38)\\\\n\\\\n- Pause Thursday hills/tempo rotation until Achilles is cleared by a clinician and symptom-free for 7+ days\\\\n- Shelve Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 until Achilles symptoms resolve; daily miles in Brooks Ghost 16 only\\\\n- Long run governed by symptoms this week — distance ceiling 8 mi, no MP finishes until further notice\\\\n- Add a daily morning Achilles check (stairs / single-leg calf raise / stiffness trend) as the go/no-go for each run\\\\n- Revisit the 3:30 goal after we have 2 clean weeks post-clearance — may need to adjust goal or race plan\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W39)\\\\n\\\\n- Keep Thursday quality rotation paused through W39; earliest return is W40 and only with clinician clearance + 7 clean days\\\\n- Keep Endorphin Speed 4 shelved; Ghost 16 only until quality returns\\\\n- Formally revisit 3:30 goal after W40 — current working range 3:35–3:38 pending clean build\\\\n- Keep daily morning Achilles check as the per-run go/no-go\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W40 (Mon Sep 28 – Sun Oct 4, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 43.98 mi | 34.83 mi | 30.66 mi | +13.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 36m | 5h 20m | 4h 45m | +1h 51m |\\\\n| Tota