Run — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 76.1% · Z3 23.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑230 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 78\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 27 — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:12/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ +3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi ▁▅▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 143 → 144 ▁▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi █▃▁▃\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Nothing. I kept checking for the Achilles on the tempo and it was fine.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Relieved and ready to build again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is there anything I should keep doing for the Achilles through race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nReally encouraging week. You held the easy-only guardrails, built back to 26 mi across 5 runs, and the Achilles went from \\\\\\"slight tightness first half mile\\\\\\" Tue → \\\\\\"a hint at the start\\\\\\" Wed → \\\\\\"fine on the flat\\\\\\" Thu → nothing Sat or Sun, no post-run stiffness. That's the trajectory we wanted. We're now 8 weeks out from Lakeshore (Nov 15). This week we build cautiously — still easy-only, Ghost 16 only, daily morning Achilles check as the go/no-go, and we nudge the long run from 8 to 10. No hills, no tempo, no MP touches yet.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Still no clinician check-in on record.** The W38 note was explicit: hills/tempo rotation stays paused until you've been cleared by a clinician AND been symptom-free for 7+ days. You've got a strong week of symptom-free running, but I don't want to add intensity on the back of self-clearance alone. See the callout — please get it looked at this week if you haven't.\\\\n- **Easy pace creeping down** (9:34 → 9:30 → 9:23 → 9:24/mi at HR 143–144). Good aerobic sign, but on a healing Achilles I'd rather you stay honest-easy and let pace be the output. Don't chase Wednesday's 9:15s.\\\\n- **Wednesday run drifted to Z3** (15.7% Z3, avg HR 148). Fine in isolation but it's the day easy becomes \\\\\\"steady.\\\\\\" Keep HR ≤148 this Wednesday.\\\\n- Sleep 7.5, strength 2/2, stress low — all green.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n**1. When can I do a hard session again?**\\\\nThe gate is unchanged: clinician clearance + 7 consecutive symptom-free days (no stiffness on morning stairs, no tightness in the first mile, nothing after the run). You've just completed what looks like your first clean week — so the earliest a quality session comes back is W40, and only if W39 is also clean AND you've got clearance. When we re-introduce, it'll be a soft return: a short strides-only session or a 2 × 1 mi at MP, not straight back into hills or a 4-mile tempo.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Does the missed week change what's realistic for race day?**\\\\nHonest answer: probably, yes. We're 8 weeks out and we've lost the Thursday quality rotation for ~3 weeks. 3:30 required MP work compounded over months — the fitness you built through W36 (that MP block at 7:58/mi) is still in the bank, but we need 4–5 clean MP sessions and 2–3 big long runs with MP finishes to sharpen it, and we don't have room for all of that now. My read: **3:35–3:38 is a realistic A-goal if the next two weeks are clean and quality returns in W40**, with 3:30 moved to a stretch \\\\\\"if the day is perfect\\\\\\" target. Let's make the call formally after W40 — I need to see one quality session back on the legs before I commit to a race plan.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **~31 mi, all easy, Ghost 16 only.** +5 mi on last week is a sensible step; we're not rushing back to 40.\\\\n- **Thursday stays flat and easy** (not the hilly route). Hilly route returns only when quality returns.\\\\n- **Long run to 10 mi**, by HR, no MP finish. Within last week's ceiling philosophy but a modest extension because you had zero symptoms Sat/Sun.\\\\n- **Daily morning Achilles check stays in** as the go/no-go. If stairs or single-leg calf raise are stiff/painful, swap that day for rest and tell me.\\\\n- **Strength both sessions** — calf raises and slow heel drops are directly protective here.\\\\n- **Wednesday stays honest-easy** (HR ≤148, slow down if needed).\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Morning Achilles check: stairs + single-leg calf raise. Note anything that isn't neutral.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:30/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on the flat canal path. First mile deliberately slow — this is also the Achilles warm-up test. If anything beyond mild first-half-mile tightness, cut short and tell me.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Go/no-go = morning Achilles check. Properly easy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: slow heel drops (straight + bent knee, 3×15 each side), single-leg calf raises, glute bridges, side plank\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi steady aerobic on the canal. Keep HR ≤148 — if it drifts into Z3 by mile 4, back off pace. Don't chase last Wednesday's splits.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Mid-week aerobic anchor. HR is the governor.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:30/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy on the FLAT canal — not the hilly route. No strides, no pickups. Just honest aerobic miles.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Normally the quality day. Stays easy and flat until Achilles is cleared by a clinician and we've got 7+ fully clean days.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤145\\",\\"distanceM\\":4828,\\"structure\\":\\"3 mi truly easy pre-long shakeout. Short on purpose.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short shakeout. If anything isn't right, swap for rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: heel drops, single-leg calf raises, core — the Achilles/shin insurance session\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤148 avg; pace is the output\\",\\"distanceM\\":16093,\\"structure\\":\\"10 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148. No MP finish this week. If anything in the Achilles flares during the run — tightness that doesn't ease by mile 2, any sharpness, any limp — stop and walk home. Fuel: gel pre-run and one at mile 5, water throughout.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Modest extension from last week's 8. The win is a clean run, not a fast one.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W39\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"785715c9-e1fa-4a05-a805-9fc07672efaa\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 52\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. When can I do a hard session again?\\\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nWe're pulling the handbrake this week. Your right Achilles went from \\\\\\"tight\\\\\\" during Thursday's tempo (sharp enough to stop at mile 2 and walk home) to stiff on Saturday to stiff-after-sitting on Sunday. That pattern — stiffness that eases with movement but keeps showing up — is a classic Achilles warning sign, and the smart move 9 weeks out from Lakeshore is to back off *now*, get it looked at by a qualified sports physio or sports-med doc, and protect the block. One cautious week costs you nothing. A stubborn Achilles pushed through costs you the race.\\\\n\\\\n## Answers to your questions\\\\n**1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?**\\\\nShort answer: a few true easy days are okay *if* the Achilles passes a simple morning check — but no quality, no long run as planned, and we abort any run the moment it talks back. The specific test each morning:\\\\n- Can you walk down the stairs normally without a sharp pinch?\\\\n- Can you do 10 single-leg calf raises on the right side without sharp pain (dull \\\\\\"I feel it\\\\\\" is fine, sharp is not)?\\\\n- Is morning stiffness the same or less than the day before?\\\\n\\\\nIf yes to all three → short, flat, slow easy run is on. If no to any → that day becomes rest or a 30-min bike/pool session instead. No negotiating.\\\\n\\\\n**2. How do I know if this is serious?**\\\\nI'm a coach, not a clinician, so I can't diagnose this — and that's exactly why I want you to see a sports physio or sports-med doctor this week, ideally in the next couple of days. The signs that mean *stop running and get seen urgently*: sharp pain that makes you limp or change your gait, visible swelling or a lump on the tendon, a feeling of weakness pushing off, pain that wakes you at night, or anything that feels like a \\\\\\"pop.\\\\\\" Getting hands on it early is the single best thing you can do for your race.\\\\n\\\\n## What I'm changing this week\\\\n- **No tempo, no MP, no strides, no hills.** Quality is off the table until the Achilles is quiet and a professional has cleared you.\\\\n- **Long run is cut to 8 miles max, flat, by feel.** Not 17 (which is where the ramp was headed). We don't lose fitness in one easy week — we lose it over three injured weeks.\\\\n- **Mileage ~18–22 mi** (down from 31). All Brooks Ghost, no Endorphin Speed (carbon plate + aggressive geometry is not what a cranky Achilles wants right now).\\\\n- **Two optional cross-training swaps** (bike or pool) if the morning check fails.\\\\n- **Daily calf care**: gentle calf stretching (straight + bent knee) 2× day, and if your physio approves, slow eccentric heel drops are the gold-standard homework — but let them prescribe those, not me.\\\\n\\\\nThe goal this week is simple: finish Sunday with the Achilles quieter than Monday. If we get that, next week we start carefully reintroducing structure. If we don't, we extend the easy block another week. We will not do another real quality session until this is settled.\\\\n\\\\nSend me a quick note mid-week on how Tuesday and Wednesday feel, and tell me what the physio says.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day + full rest. Gentle calf stretching 2× (straight-knee and bent-knee, 30s × 3 each side). Book the physio/sports-med appointment today if you haven't.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45–10:00/mi, HR ≤145\\",\\"distanceM\\":4828,\\"structure\\":\\"Only if the morning Achilles check passes. 3 mi very easy on the flat canal — no hills, no strides. Abort immediately if sharp pain or if you catch yourself favoring the leg. If check fails: 30 min easy stationary bike instead.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This is a test run, not a training run. Finish feeling like you could have done more.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:45/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"Only if morning check passes AND Tuesday ran clean. 4 mi flat and easy. Stop if the Achilles sharpens at any point.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"If Tuesday wasn't clean, swap to 30–40 min bike or pool run.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Deliberately rest today — this slot was tempo/MP in the old rotation. Not this week. Optional 30 min easy bike or pool run if you want aerobic time. No running.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Keep up calf stretching.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:50/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi flat and easy, pre-'long' shakeout. Morning check must pass. Abort on any sharp pain.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-19\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"By feel, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"UP TO 8 mi, flat, by feel. Not the planned 17. No MP, no strong finish, no hills. If the Achilles starts talking in the first 2 miles, turn around and come home — that's the right answer, not a failure. Fuel practice is still welcome (gel ~mile 4) since it costs the Achilles nothing.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Goal of this run: finish with the Achilles no worse than it started. If physio says shorter, do shorter.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W38\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"3c7734eb-98fd-4127-a3bb-52042324cf03\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W37 (Mon Sep 7 – Sun Sep 13, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 31.22 mi | 44.41 mi | 40.23 mi | -9.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 51m | 6h 49m | 6h 17m | -1h 26m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 955 ft | 843 ft | -98 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 225 | 328 | 314 | -89 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.5%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████████░░░░░  87.1%   (4h 14m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  9.3%   (27m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.1%   (6m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **88.64%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 8 — Easy Run — 6.03 mi / 56m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑167 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 9 — Easy Run — 8.20 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.1 → 150.2 (+4.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.7% · Z3 9.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 10 — Tempo Run — 3.10 mi / 28m 1s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 145 (77.1% max)  ·  Max HR 177  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:36/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 133.5 → 169.4 (+35.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 7.1% · Z2 66% · Z3 5.4% · Z4 21.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑10 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Right Achilles tight from mile 2. Stopped at 3.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 3/10  ·  Pain: Right Achilles tight from about mile 2 of the session. Got sharper as I picked up the pace, so I stopped at 3 miles and walked home.\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 12 — Easy Run — 3.89 mi / 37m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:36/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 144 (+6.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.7% · Z2 97.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 5/10  ·  Pain: Achilles stiff for the first mile, eased after that. About a 3 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 13 — Long Run — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 79.7% · Z3 19.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 65\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: No pain while running. Stiff getting out of the car afterwards.\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 13 — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:16/mi vs front 9:18/mi (vs front half; Δ +2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi █▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7 hrs (range 6.2–7.7)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped the second one to rest the legs.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Worried about the Achilles.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Right Achilles, just above the heel. Tight and a bit tender to press. No swelling that I can see. It was fine until the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Anxious. I don't want to throw away the block over this.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\n2. How do I know if this is serious?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nThat was a breakthrough week — 44.4 mi, a 16-miler with a genuine MP finish (7:58, 7:55 at the end of a long run), and you came out of it confident. We're 10 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week I want to keep the shape but not stack another mileage jump on top of last week's +6.4. We hold ~42 mi, Thursday rotates back to hills (per the rotation), and Sunday is 17 by HR with a shorter MP touch at the end. First real test of fueling, too.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Long-run HR drift was +13.4 bpm** on Sunday (143.5 → 156.9, with Z4 time in the MP finish). Above our ≤10 bpm target. Some of that is the MP close, some is accumulated load from a big week. We'll govern the easy portion by HR cap 148 again and keep the MP piece shorter this week.\\\\n- **Mileage jump last week was ~+6 mi** on the prior week. Another +6 this week would be the exact setup where your shins got cranky in your first block. Holding flat at ~42 mi is deliberate.\\\\n- **No body complaints beyond \\\\\\"heavy legs\\\\\\"** post-long — that's normal. Just want it noted so you flag anything sharper.\\\\n- Sleep 7.2 hr, strength 2/2 — all green.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — gel on the long run?\\\\nYes. Now is the right time to start practicing. The rule for marathon day is \\\\\\"nothing new on race day,\\\\\\" which means we practice fueling in training for the next 8 weeks. Start simple:\\\\n- **One gel 10–15 min before you head out** (with water).\\\\n- **One gel at ~mile 6**, another at **~mile 11** on Sunday's 17.\\\\n- Wash each one down with a few sips of water — gels need fluid to absorb cleanly.\\\\n- Pick a brand you can get at the race expo or carry yourself. Try one brand this week, note how your stomach handles it, and we'll iterate.\\\\nTarget is ~30–60g carbs per hour on race day; two gels across a 17-miler gets you in the ballpark without overloading your gut while you're still learning.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Hold volume ~42 mi** to absorb last week's load before pushing again in W38.\\\\n- **Thursday = hills** per the rotation. 8 × 60–75 sec uphill. Builds strength and leg stiffness, kinder to the system than another MP block right after Sunday's finish.\\\\n- **Sunday long = 17 mi, HR-capped easy with last 3 at MP effort.** Shorter MP block than last Sunday (3 vs the extended Z3/Z4 segment that drove the drift). We're protecting the drift number while still touching goal pace.\\\\n- **Easy days properly easy** — Wednesday has been creeping into Z3; keep HR ≤150 even if that means slowing to 9:30+.\\\\n- **Both strength sessions** since you're home all week.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Walk/mobility if you want.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:30/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational + 4×20s relaxed strides on flat at the end\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake out Sunday's 16. Strides keep turnover sharp.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady aerobic on canal. If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 5, back off — don't chase the pace you had last Wednesday.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Mid-week aerobic anchor. Properly easy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Reps by effort (RPE 8); recoveries easy Z1–Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"1.5 mi easy WU → drills → 8 × 60–75s UPHILL strong (not sprint) w/ easy jog-down recovery (~2 min) → 1.5 mi CD. ~7 mi total on the Thursday hilly route.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Hills this week per the Thursday rotation. Tempo/MP returns W38. Effort self-regulated — the hill caps the top end so you can't blow it up.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi truly easy, pre-long shakeout\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-12\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core — the shin insurance session\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy portion HR ≤148; MP close 8:00–8:10/mi, HR ≤164\\",\\"distanceM\\":27359,\\"structure\\":\\"17 mi: first 14 easy at HR cap 148 (pace will be ~9:30–9:45). Last 3 mi at MP effort (8:00–8:10/mi, HR ≤164). If HR is already drifting hard by mile 10, drop the MP finish and just finish easy — tell me after.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fueling practice: gel 10–15 min pre-run, gel at mile 6, gel at mile 11. Water with each. Carry fluids given the distance.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W37\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W42\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-19T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-10-12\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-10-18\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "xhigh"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRfirJQLY8MSBtEakJDT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm reviewing the training context: after W41's 20-miler with marathon-pace work, I need to plan W42, which the coach's guidance pegs at roughly 44 miles with an 18-miler including 4 miles at marathon pace, building toward the Nov 15 Lakeshore Marathon.\\n\\nMapping out the week, Monday is travel/rest, Tuesday and Wednesday are easy runs, Thursday is the quality day, Friday rests again for travel, Saturday is easy, and Sunday holds the long run. I'm checking the Thursday workout rotation pattern — W40 had marathon-pace tempo work, but W41 actually came in as an interval session (5x~1k at 6:55-7:02 pace) rather than the planned MP work, so I'm noting that W42's Thursday should likely rotate back to MP/tempo to stay on track with the build toward W43's peak week and the eventual 3:30 vs 3:35 race-pace decision.\\n\\nTurning to the athlete's actual questions, they're asking whether 3:30 is still realistic and whether heavy legs the day after a 20-miler is normal. I'm reviewing the concerning metrics from this block: long run HR drift hit +16.9 bpm again (over the ≤10 bpm target), relative effort spiked to 340 versus a 254 three-week average suggesting overload, easy-run HR held steady at 144, but time in Z1+Z2 dropped to just 68.7% against an 80% target — likely due to the hard Thursday intervals plus MP work in the long run. Strength training was only 1 of 2 sessions, and sleep dipped to 6.8 hours from 7.5, which all points to some accumulated fatigue going into this next build week.\\n\\nStill, there's good news: heavy legs after a 20-miler is expected, and the Achilles held up fine. The MP pace data is encouraging too — 3:30 marathon pace is 8:00/mile, and the 20-miler's MP finish segments landed right at 7:58-8:04/mile, confirming that goal is on track.\\n\\nNow I'm planning out Week 42 at 44 miles with the 18-mile long run including 4 at MP, plus the Thursday tempo session, while being mindful of the drift issue and trying to push the Z1+Z2 percentage back up. I'm starting to lay out each day — rest Monday for travel, easy Tuesday and Wednesday runs...\\n\\nThursday's MP tempo needs more thought - I'm weighing different structures like a warmup plus continuous MP miles versus broken-up MP segments with jog recovery, trying to hit the right weekly mileage total around 44-45 miles while keeping the session effective for marathon pace work.\\n\\nRounding out the week totals 45 miles. Now I'm assessing the overall picture: a strong 20-miler with the Achilles staying quiet and the 3:30 pace handled cleanly in the MP segment is a good sign, though HR drift was elevated again (+16.9 bpm) and sleep dipped to 6.8 hours. Easy-run HR stayed steady at 144, but Z1+Z2 time came in below target at 68.7%, and I'm noting that strength training got skipped Friday.\\n\\nOn the pacing question, hitting 7:58-8:04 for the MP finish after 17 easy miles confirms 3:30 is still realistic, though I want to hold the final decision until after W43's 20-miler with 5 MP miles - keeping the working range at 3:30-3:35. Heavy legs post-long-run are expected given it's the longest effort in two years, and shouldn't be a concern unless it lingers past 48 hours, in which case I'd cut strides on Tuesday. No acute safety flags here, so I'll move on to drafting the submission.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hqqhwb5uHeu6b8RKDLUkqF","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nThat was a milestone week. 45 miles, your longest training run in two years, and the last 4 miles clipped off at 7:58–8:04/mi — right on 3:30 pace — at the end of a 20-miler. The Achilles stayed quiet. That's the single best data point we've generated this block. We're 4 weeks out from Lakeshore (Nov 15). W42 is a build week per the shape I've been building toward: **~45 mi, long run 18 w/ 4 at marathon pace**, Thursday back to a continuous MP tempo. W43 is the peak (20 w/ 5 MP) and that's where we formally lock the race-pace decision.\\n\\n## Your questions\\n**1. Is 3:30 still sensible after this block?**\\nIt's in play. The honest answer: the last 4 miles of Sunday's 20 came in at 7:58–8:04/mi, which IS 3:30 pace, and you held it on tired legs after 17 easy miles. That's the single thing I most wanted to see. BUT — your HR drifted +16.9 bpm across the run (above our ≤10 target), and the MP finish spent real time in Z4. That tells me 3:30 at the end of 20 is on the edge, not comfortable. The call stays: working range **3:30–3:35**, locked formally after W43's 20 w/ 5 at MP. If W43 looks like Sunday did — pace clean but drift ugly — I'll steer us to 3:33–3:35 as the A-goal with 3:30 as a \\"if the day is perfect\\" stretch. If drift comes down and 5 MP miles feel honest, 3:30 is on.\\n\\n**2. Is heavy legs on Monday normal after a 20?**\\nYes — especially the longest run you've done in two years. Expect 48 hours of thick legs; Tuesday's easy run should feel better by mile 2, and by Wednesday you should feel normal. If legs are still dead Tuesday evening, skip the strides and run shorter. The useful heavy-legs signal to watch for is a joint or tendon that feels different, not general muscle fatigue — that's just the long run working.\\n\\n## Concerns / flags\\n- **Long-run drift was +16.9 bpm again** (144.5 → 161.4). That's two long runs in a row above the ≤10 target. Partly explained by the MP finish, partly by cumulative load, maybe partly by fuel/hydration late. This week we govern the easy portion of the long run strictly by HR cap 148 and shorten the MP finish to 4 miles. If drift stays this high in W43, we adjust the race plan, not the training.\\n- **Sleep dipped to 6.8 hr** (from 7.5). Minor, but worth flagging four weeks out — this is when sleep matters most. Target 7+ this week.\\n- **Z1+Z2 was 68.7%** — below the 80% target. Driven by a hot Thursday interval session (that landed heavier than planned) plus the MP finish. This week's Thursday is MP tempo, not intervals, and Wednesday needs to be honest-easy (HR cap 148) — it's been drifting toward \\"steady.\\"\\n- **Strength 1/2** — understand the travel reality. Please get both in this week; the calf/single-leg work is cheap insurance.\\n- **Achilles**: silent through Sunday's 20. Daily morning check continues through race day as agreed — stairs, 10 single-leg calf raises, stiffness scan. Non-negotiable.\\n\\n## This week — the \\"why\\"\\n- **Tue easy 6 + strides**: shake out Sunday's legs, 4×20s strides reintroduce turnover before Thursday's MP work.\\n- **Wed easy 8**: aerobic anchor. **HR cap 148.** If pace drops to 9:30+ to hold that, that's correct. Don't chase.\\n- **Thu MP tempo (8 mi)**: 1.5 WU + 5 mi continuous @ MP (8:00–8:05/mi, HR cap 164) + 1.5 CD. This is the big quality session of the week — doing 5 continuous MP miles mid-week sets up the 4 MP miles at the end of Sunday's long run.\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\n- **Sun long 18 w/ 4 at MP**: first 14 easy by HR cap 148 (expect ~9:20–9:35), last 4 at MP effort (8:00–8:05/mi, HR cap 164). Shorter easy portion than last week but same MP finish length — this is the dress rehearsal for W43's peak.\\n- **Strength 2×** — the calf/single-leg insurance session.\\n- **Fueling**: gel 10–15 min pre-long, gel at mile 5, mile 10, mile 14 (right before the MP block). Water with each. Same brand/flavor you plan to use race day — no experiments this close in.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W42","days":[{"date":"2026-10-12","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Morning Achilles check (stairs + single-leg calf raises). Walk and mobility are fine. Hydrate well — you're coming off a 20."},{"date":"2026-10-13","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":9656,"paceOrHr":"~9:20/mi, HR ≤148","structure":"6 mi conversational on the flat canal + 4×20s relaxed strides on flat ground at the end. Strides smooth, not sprinty.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"If legs still feel dead from Sunday's 20, drop the strides and come home at 5 mi — tell me how it felt.","strength":"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent knee, 3×12 slow eccentric), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges — the Achilles insurance session"},{"date":"2026-10-14","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":12875,"paceOrHr":"Z2, HR ≤148","structure":"8 mi steady aerobic on the canal. Keep HR ≤148 — if it drifts into Z3 by mile 5, back off. Pace is the output, HR is the governor.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"This has been drifting toward 'steady' — keep it honest-easy this week. 9:30/mi at HR 146 is correct; 9:07/mi at HR 150 is not."},{"date":"2026-10-15","dayType":"quality","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":12875,"paceOrHr":"WU/CD Z2; MP block 8:00–8:05/mi, HR ≤164","structure":"8 mi MP tempo: 1.5 mi easy WU + drills → 5 mi continuous at marathon pace (8:00–8:05/mi, HR cap 164) → 1.5 mi easy CD. Flat canal, no hills.","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4"},"notes":"The big session of the week. Dress rehearsal for Sunday's MP finish. If MP block average HR goes over 164 before mile 3, back the pace off 5 sec/mi — don't force 8:00 at the cost of control. Report back on how clean the pace felt."},{"date":"2026-10-16","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel day — full rest. Morning Achilles check. Stretch calves."},{"date":"2026-10-17","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"~9:40/mi, HR ≤148","structure":"5 mi truly easy, pre-long shakeout. Z2 only.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"20–30 min: calves (slow eccentric heel drops), single-leg work, core"},{"date":"2026-10-18","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":28968,"paceOrHr":"Easy portion HR ≤148 (pace will be ~9:20–9:35); MP block 8:00–8:05/mi, HR ≤164","structure":"18 mi: first 14 easy by HR cap 148. Last 4 mi at marathon pace (8:00–8:05/mi, HR cap 164). If HR is drifting hard by mile 10 — up 8+ bpm from start — drop the MP finish to 2 mi or jog it in, and tell me.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Fueling: gel 10–15 min pre-run, gel at mile 5, gel at mile 10, gel at mile 14 (right before the MP block). Water with each. Same brand you plan to use race day. This is the dress rehearsal for W43's peak long run."}]},"settingsProposalBullets":["Lock race-pace decision formally after W43 long run (20 w/ 5 MP); current working range 3:30–3:35 pending drift behavior.","If W43 long-run drift stays >12 bpm, steer race plan toward 3:33–3:35 with 3:30 as a stretch 'perfect day' target.","Keep daily morning Achilles check through race day as the per-run go/no-go.","Watch sleep — flag if weekly average drops below 7 hr again in the final 4 weeks.","W44 opens the taper; W45 mid-taper; W46 race week."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28105,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5608,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2164}},"diagnostics":null}	200	77924	tool_use	28105	5608	0	0	ok	\N	2164
4d1276ac-34a3-48fb-b27f-aa41a3b0d9a4	2026-10-13 00:10:21.916017+00	mid_week_chat	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	ade95529-4867-48ab-9d41-47ec2590ab7b	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_mid_week_chat_reply", "description": "Submit the mid-week coach reply (attached-run feedback and optional remaining-day plan patches when present).", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string", "description": "Athlete-facing mid-week coach prose. When attachments are present, include concrete run feedback from metrics/splits."}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "allowPastDayPatches": {"type": "boolean", "description": "When true, past-day patches may be applied. Default false — past days stay stable."}, "prescribedDayPatches": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD within the plan week"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Optional day replacements for remaining plan days (date >= local today). Full PrescribedDay objects."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets when the mid-week note is a significant memory update. Never silent-apply."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach answering a mid-week check-in. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. When workout attachments are present, give concrete coaching feedback on those runs using metrics and splits only (no GPS or route geometry). When the athlete asks to change remaining plan days, emit prescribedDayPatches with full day objects for those dates only (do not rewrite past days unless allowPastDayPatches is true). Do not rewrite the full week plan unless asked. For significant memory updates, emit settingsProposalBullets (soft-gate); never silent-apply dossier changes. Think it through first, then call the submit_mid_week_chat_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Call the submit_mid_week_chat_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nNo workout attachments — answer the athlete's mid-week note.\\nCurrent prescribed week is in the packet. To change remaining days, emit prescribedDayPatches using only these dates: 2026-10-12, 2026-10-13, 2026-10-14, 2026-10-15, 2026-10-16, 2026-10-17, 2026-10-18. Past days stay stable unless allowPastDayPatches is true.\\nDo not rewrite the full prescribed week unless the athlete asks.\\nWhen the athlete reports a significant memory update (new constraint, niggle, schedule change), populate settingsProposalBullets for soft-gate Accept — never mutate the dossier directly.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":7,\\"body\\":\\"# About you (v1)\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sunday Nov 15. It will be my fourth marathon. My best is 3:41 from two years ago and I want to run 3:30 this time.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nI run Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are off because of work travel. Weekday runs are early, around 6, before work, so about an hour at most. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Roughly 6 to 7 hours a week, and more on long-run weeks. I took it easy in June and have been back at about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\n## Constraints\\\\nNothing right now. I had shin splints in my first marathon block, so I tend to ramp up carefully. I can't move the Monday and Friday rest days, and I travel for work about one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, one hillier route on Thursdays. Sunday long run. I like to know why a session is in the plan. I'm happy to run hard on quality days but I want the easy days to be properly easy. Brooks Ghost for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## From your running log\\\\n- Units: imperial\\\\n- HR zones: Z1 112–131; Z2 131–150; Z3 150–164; Z4 164–177; Z5 177–188\\\\n- Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n- Recent training: Long run 11 (10.8 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi); Easy 6 (5.8 mi); Medium-long 6 (6.2 mi); Easy 5 (4.9 mi)\\\\n\\\\n## Coaching notes\\\\nProtect easy days. Cap quality when constraints are present. Revisit this brief after week one.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W33)\\\\n\\\\n- Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next\\\\n- Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker\\\\n- Revisit goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Thursday rotation this week: hills (tempo/MP returns W35)\\\\n- Long run governed by HR cap 148 while heat persists\\\\n- Mileage target ~40 mi, +~6% on W33\\\\n- Revisit 3:30 goal pace realism in late September\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W38)\\\\n\\\\n- Pause Thursday hills/tempo rotation until Achilles is cleared by a clinician and symptom-free for 7+ days\\\\n- Shelve Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 until Achilles symptoms resolve; daily miles in Brooks Ghost 16 only\\\\n- Long run governed by symptoms this week — distance ceiling 8 mi, no MP finishes until further notice\\\\n- Add a daily morning Achilles check (stairs / single-leg calf raise / stiffness trend) as the go/no-go for each run\\\\n- Revisit the 3:30 goal after we have 2 clean weeks post-clearance — may need to adjust goal or race plan\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W39)\\\\n\\\\n- Keep Thursday quality rotation paused through W39; earliest return is W40 and only with clinician clearance + 7 clean days\\\\n- Keep Endorphin Speed 4 shelved; Ghost 16 only until quality returns\\\\n- Formally revisit 3:30 goal after W40 — current working range 3:35–3:38 pending clean build\\\\n- Keep daily morning Achilles check as the per-run go/no-go\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W41)\\\\n\\\\n- Lock 3:30 vs 3:35 race-pace decision formally after W43 long run (20 mi w/ 5 at MP)\\\\n- Target shape: W42 build (~44 mi, 18 w/ 4 MP), W43 peak (~46 mi, 20 w/ 5 MP), W44 taper opens, W45 mid-taper, W46 race week\\\\n- Keep daily morning Achilles check through race day as a cheap insurance habit\\\\n- Reinforce easy-day HR cap 148 on Wednesday — easy has been drifting steady\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W42)\\\\n\\\\n- Lock race-pace decision formally after W43 long run (20 w/ 5 MP); current working range 3:30–3:35 pending drift behavior.\\\\n- If W43 long-run drift stays >12 bpm, steer race plan toward 3:33–3:35 with 3:30 as a stretch 'perfect day' target.\\\\n- Keep daily morning Achilles check through race day as the per-run go/no-go.\\\\n- Watch sleep — flag if weekly average drops below 7 hr again in the final 4 weeks.\\\\n- W44 opens the taper; W45 mid-taper; W46 race week.\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":null,\\"thread\\":[{\\"role\\":\\"athlete\\",\\"body\\":\\"Legs are heavy today after the 20 miler. Tuesday is an easy 6 as planned. Is it fine to keep it properly slow?\\",\\"createdAt\\":\\"2026-10-26T22:53:19.498Z\\"}],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W42\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-19T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"ade95529-4867-48ab-9d41-47ec2590ab7b\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W41\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"ce494be1-dde2-4543-90a9-fa6879bac4e3\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W41 (Mon Oct 5 – Sun Oct 11, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.97 mi | 43.98 mi | 34.92 mi | +10.1 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 40m | 6h 36m | 5h 20m | +1h 20m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 787 ft | 678 ft | +277 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 340 | 317 | 254 | +86 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (6m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░  67.3%   (4h 30m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  16.7%   (1h 7m)\\\\nZ4 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  10.7%   (43m)\\\\nZ5 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  3.9%   (16m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **68.7%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Oct 6 — Easy Run — 4.88 mi / 45m 7s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:15/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.6 → 143.9 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.3% · Z2 96.7% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑89 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Oct 7 — Easy Run — 7.94 mi / 1h 12m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:07/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146 → 149.8 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 95.2% · Z3 4.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑220 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 51\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Oct 8 — Interval Run — 8.11 mi / 1h 5m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 163 (86.7% max)  ·  Max HR 184  ·  Cad 354 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 7:02/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:57/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:55/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:57/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:58/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 150.9 → 155.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.1% · Z2 25.5% · Z3 13.1% · Z4 34.6% · Z5 23.8%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑164 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 104\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 9/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Oct 10 — Easy Run — 3.96 mi / 36m 45s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 143.9 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 4.1% · Z2 95.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑72 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Oct 11 — Long Run — 20.09 mi / 3h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 169  ·  Cad 347 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 7:58/mi / 8:03/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.5 → 161.4 (+16.9 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 58.2% · Z3 30.3% · Z4 11.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑410 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 127\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Oct 11 — 20.09 mi / 3h 1m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 151  ·  Drift: 144.5 → 161.4 (+16.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 7:58/mi / 8:03/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 8:45/mi vs front 9:13/mi (faster than front half by 28s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi → 9:12/mi ▁▃██ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi → 20.09 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (340) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (254) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.8 hrs (range 6–7.5)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs heavy, especially after the 20 miler. The Achilles was fine the whole way.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Tired but pleased. The 20 miler was the longest training run I've done in two years.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is my 3:30 target still sensible after this block?\\\\n2. Is heavy legs on Monday normal after a 20 miler?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBig week, well executed. 44 mi, 17-miler with a crisp MP close (7:60/8:03/8:04 — right on 3:30 pace), Achilles stayed quiet, and you came off it saying you could have held MP longer. That's the exact signal we needed. **3:30 is back on the table as a realistic A-goal**, provided the next two build weeks land clean. But right now, 6 weeks out, we don't stack another big one — we take a step back this week, let the load settle, then build to peak over W42–W43 before taper.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Long-run HR drift was +15.9 bpm** (144 → 160). Target is ≤10. Part of that is the MP finish, part is a 17-miler stacked on top of a +9 mi weekly jump. Not alarming on its own — but combined with the overload flag below, it's the clearest \\\\\\"cutback this week\\\\\\" signal.\\\\n- **Relative effort 317 vs 3-wk avg 223** — the report flagged possible overload. You feel fine, which is great; the data wants a down week anyway. The best weeks come after true recovery, not after stacked big ones.\\\\n- **Easy-run creep continues** — Wednesday drifted into Z3 again (avg HR 148, max 153, splits in the 9:0x range when HR said 9:15–9:20). Keep Wednesday properly easy this week with a hard HR cap at 148.\\\\n- **Shin-splint history + Achilles context** — both are reasons to respect the cutback and not freelance miles upward. Achilles has been quiet across W39 and W40, which is exactly what we wanted. Keep the morning check as your per-run go/no-go.\\\\n- Sleep 7.5, strength 2/2, stress low, legs tired-not-sore — all green otherwise.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — how should the final weeks look?\\\\nHere's the shape from here to the line (Sun Nov 15):\\\\n\\\\n- **W41 (this week, Oct 5–11)**: Cutback — ~38 mi, long 14, Thursday tempo (shorter MP block than last week). *Purpose: absorb last week, let the drift reset.*\\\\n- **W42 (Oct 12–18)**: Build — ~44 mi, long 18 with 4 mi at MP. *First \\\\\\"race-rehearsal\\\\\\" long run.*\\\\n- **W43 (Oct 19–25)**: **Peak week** — ~46 mi, long 20 with 5 mi at MP finish. *Biggest run and biggest week of the block.*\\\\n- **W44 (Oct 26–Nov 1)**: Taper opens — ~38 mi, long 15 with 3 mi MP. *Volume starts coming down, intensity stays.*\\\\n- **W45 (Nov 2–8)**: Mid-taper — ~28 mi, long 12 easy, one short tempo (~3 mi). *Legs recover; sharpness kept with short efforts.*\\\\n- **W46 (Nov 9–15, race week)**: ~15–18 mi before race. Mon off, Tue easy 4 + 4 strides, Wed easy 5, Thu easy 4 w/ 3×1 min at MP, Fri rest, Sat shakeout 2 mi, **Sun race**.\\\\n\\\\nFormal 3:30 vs 3:35 call: I'll lock the race pace plan after W43's long run. If 20 miles with 5 at MP (8:00/mi, HR ≤164) feels controlled and the drift behaves, we commit to 3:30. If it's a grind, we start at 3:35 pace and race the back half.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **~38 mi, down from 44.** A proper cutback, not a hold. The drift and overload flag both earned it.\\\\n- **Thursday = tempo intervals, not hills.** 2×2 mi at MP with a short jog between — teaches re-engaging MP effort, which is the race-specific skill. Shorter total MP volume than last week (4 mi vs 4 mi, but broken) to go easier on the system during the cutback.\\\\n- **Long run cut to 14, no MP finish.** Pure aerobic by HR. We're letting the system reset so W42's 18 with MP finish is clean. Not a loss — a setup.\\\\n- **Wednesday is HR-governed (≤148).** If the splits say 9:00 but HR says 150, slow down.\\\\n- **Shoes**: Ghost 16 for daily, Endorphin Speed 4 for Thursday only.\\\\n- **Both strength sessions in** — calf work is still Achilles insurance.\\\\n- **Keep the morning Achilles check**. It's been clean for weeks; let's not drop the habit until after race day.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-05\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Quick morning Achilles check (stairs + single-leg calf raise) stays on.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:20/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi conversational on the flat canal + 4 × 20s relaxed strides on flat at the end (full walk/jog recovery between). Strides keep turnover sharp without stressing anything.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-06\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: slow heel drops (straight + bent knee, 3×15 each side), single-leg calf raises, glute bridges, side plank\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤148 (hard cap)\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady aerobic on canal. HARD HR cap 148 — if HR drifts into Z3 by mile 4, slow down even if the pace feels right. Don't chase last Wednesday's splits.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This is the day easy has been quietly becoming steady. Fix it this week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 8:00/mi, HR ≤164; recoveries easy Z1–Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi: 2 mi easy WU → 2 × 2 mi at MP (8:00/mi target, HR cap 164) w/ 3 min easy jog between → 1 mi CD. HR is the governor — if you need Z4 to hold 8:00, back off to 8:05–8:10.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shorter MP volume than last Thursday on purpose — cutback week. Flat canal, not the hilly route.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:30/mi, HR ≤145\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi truly easy pre-long shakeout. Short on purpose — this is a cutback week.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-10\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: heel drops, single-leg calf raises, core — the Achilles/shin insurance session\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤148 avg; pace is the output\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148. NO MP finish this week — all aerobic. If HR drifts into Z3 before mile 10, back off 15–20 sec/mi. Fuel practice: gel 10–15 min pre-run, gel at ~mile 5 and ~mile 10, water with each, electrolytes in the bottle.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Deliberately shorter than last Sunday's 17. The win this week is a clean aerobic 14 with drift back under control — that's what sets up a strong 18-with-MP next week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W41\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W40\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"926df228-422a-4204-bf31-375758fd30e6\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W40 (Mon Sep 28 – Sun Oct 4, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 43.98 mi | 34.83 mi | 30.66 mi | +13.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 36m | 5h 20m | 4h 45m | +1h 51m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 787 ft | 722 ft | 664 ft | +124 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 317 | 274 | 223 | +94 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.1%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  74.8%   (4h 57m)\\\\nZ3 ███████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  18.9%   (1h 15m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.1%   (20m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **75.95%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 29 — Easy Run — 5.85 mi / 54m 5s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:15/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:07/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.1 → 144 (+4.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 38\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 30 — Easy Run — 7.97 mi / 1h 12m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:07/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:06/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:02/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145 → 149.7 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 94.5% · Z3 5.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑148 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 51\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Oct 1 — Marathon Pace Run — 7.89 mi / 1h 7m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:32/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 163  ·  Cad 355 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:22/mi / 7:55/mi / 7:60/mi / 7:53/mi / 7:56/mi / 8:01/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:26/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 145.1 (+7.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.2% · Z2 39.8% · Z3 58% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑161 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 87\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Oct 3 — Easy Run — 5.09 mi / 47m 35s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:23/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.4 → 144.5 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.2% · Z2 96.8% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑92 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Oct 4 — Long Run — 17.18 mi / 2h 34m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 170  ·  Cad 347 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:01/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:15/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:03/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.3 → 160.1 (+15.9 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 65.9% · Z3 20.7% · Z4 13.2% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑279 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Oct 4 — 17.18 mi / 2h 34m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 150  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 160.1 (+15.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:01/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:15/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:03/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 8:48/mi vs front 9:10/mi (faster than front half by 23s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 143 → 144 → 144 ▁█▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi ▃▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (317) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (223) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 7–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs tired after the long run but nothing sore. Achilles quiet.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. The last three miles at marathon pace were hard but I could have held it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. How should the final weeks before the race look?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nWelcome back to a real training week. The Achilles sat quiet through a 35-mile week that included a tempo Thursday, and Sunday's 12 at HR 148 looked clean (back half a touch faster than the front — exactly what we want). With Lakeshore seven weeks out, W40 is where we rebuild structure: modest mileage bump to ~39 mi, a controlled MP tempo on Thursday, and a long run back out to 14 with a short goal-pace touch at the end.\\\\n\\\\nOne honest note: last Thursday's tempo technically beat the plan — the quality rotation was supposed to wait on clinician clearance plus 7 clean days. It went fine and the Achilles didn't flinch, which is good news. From here, please keep me posted on whether you've actually seen a physio/sports-med doc. If you have and they're happy, we're green. If you haven't, I'd still love you to book one as insurance, because we're going to progressively ask more of that tendon over the next month.\\\\n\\\\n## Concerns / flags\\\\n- **Achilles history is still recent.** Keep the morning check every day — stairs down, 10 single-leg calf raises, stiffness trend. Sharp pinch or worsening stiffness = that day's run becomes rest or a bike spin, no debate.\\\\n- **Sunday's drift was +8.8 bpm** over 12 mi — within our ≤10 target but close. Heat may still be in play. Long run stays HR-governed this week.\\\\n- **Mileage ramp:** 26 → 35 → 39 is a reasonable progression, not aggressive. We don't exceed last block's peak this week.\\\\n- **Shoe reintroduction:** Endorphin Speed 4 can come back for Thursday's workout only, since last week's session was clean. Daily miles stay in the Ghost.\\\\n- **3:30 goal:** still working range 3:35–3:38 per the W39 note. Let's see this week and next, then I'll call it. Thursday's MP work this week is at 8:05/mi (≈3:32 pace) — if that feels controlled, we're in business.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — Achilles care through race day\\\\nYes, this is now part of the plan from here to Nov 15. Three things, non-negotiable:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Daily morning check** — the same stairs / single-leg calf raise / stiffness scan. 30 seconds. Any sharp pain or worsening stiffness = that day is rest or cross-train. Tell me in the next check-in if it flares.\\\\n2. **Calf strength 2× per week** — straight-knee and bent-knee heel raises (3×12 each side), ideally slow eccentric lowers. If your physio has given you a specific heel-drop protocol, do theirs over mine.\\\\n3. **Warm up properly for quality days** — never jump straight into fast running. The 1.5–2 mi easy warm-up on workout days is the Achilles's friend. On race morning: 10 min easy walk-jog + a few relaxed strides before the gun.\\\\n\\\\nAlso: no spikes, no track flats, and keep the Endorphin Speed for workouts only — not daily miles. If anything changes, we adjust — this isn't fire-and-forget.\\\\n\\\\n## This week — the \\\\\\"why\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Tue easy 6 + strides**: shake out Sunday's long, strides reintroduce turnover before Thursday.\\\\n- **Wed easy 7**: aerobic anchor, keep HR ≤150 even if it means 9:30+ pace.\\\\n- **Thu MP tempo (7.5 mi total)**: 1.5 WU → 4 mi @ MP (8:05/mi, HR ≤164) → 2 CD. Builds goal-pace volume in a controlled block. This is kinder to the Achilles than hill reps right now, so we hold hills off one more week.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\\\\n- **Sun long 14**: first 12 easy by HR cap 148, last 2 at MP effort if HR allows. Shorter MP touch than peak training — we're rebuilding the long run, not peaking it yet.\\\\n- **Strength 2×** — the calf/single-leg session is the Achilles insurance.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Morning Achilles check. Calf stretching 2× (straight + bent knee, 30s × 3 each side).\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:20/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi conversational on the flat canal + 4×20s relaxed strides at the end on flat ground. Strides should feel smooth, not sprinty.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-29\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Morning check first. If anything sharp, swap to 30 min easy bike and text me.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calf raises (straight + bent, 3×12 slow eccentric), single-leg RDL, side plank, glute bridges — the Achilles insurance session\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Z2, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady aerobic on canal. If HR drifts into Z3 by mile 5, back off — pace is the output, HR is the governor.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-30\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"WU/CD Z2; MP block 8:05/mi, HR ≤164\\",\\"distanceM\\":12070,\\"structure\\":\\"7.5 mi MP tempo: 1.5 mi easy WU + drills → 4 mi continuous at marathon-pace effort (8:05/mi, cap HR 164) → 2 mi easy CD. Flat canal — no hills on this one.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-01\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First real MP block since the Achilles scare. If anything sharpens in the WU, abort and come home easy — this is a test session as much as a training session. Hills return in W41 if this week is clean.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-02\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel day — full rest. Keep up calf stretching.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"~9:40/mi, HR ≤148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-03\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"20–30 min: calves, single-leg work, core\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy portion HR ≤148 (pace will be ~9:20–9:35); optional last 2 mi @ MP 8:05/mi, HR ≤164\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi: first 12 easy by HR cap 148. Last 2 mi at marathon-pace effort IF HR has stayed under cap and the Achilles is quiet. If HR is drifting hard by mile 9, drop the MP finish and jog it in — tell me after.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fueling practice: gel 10–15 min pre-run, gel at mile 5, gel at mile 10. Water with each. This is a rebuild long run, not a peak — bank the clean execution.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W40\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W39\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"a5660788-041e-4bad-b5fa-c3ee40b81b12\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░