8 with minimal drift from 147 to 153, which is a clean execution — but I'm wondering if this was actually supposed to be the MP tempo session rather than an easy medium-long run, since they'd rescheduled it earlier in the week.\\n\\nActually, the shoe question matters too - the Achilles issue from W38-39 led to morning checks continuing into W41-42, and the Endorphin Speed had been shelved before being reintroduced for quality work in W40. Now the athlete wants to use the Speed shoe for both long runs (currently in the Ghost 16) and MP work going forward, which is a meaningful shift from the current plan.\\n\\nThe Achilles twinge from the latest run was noticeable for a few minutes around mile 7 of a 9-mile easy effort but settled and was nothing like the September episode -- worth flagging as a caution rather than an alarm, while keeping the morning check habit going. On the shoe switch, I want to push back on putting long runs in the carbon-plated Endorphin Speed given the Achilles history, since carbon plates alter load patterns and can mask fatigue signals.\\n\\nEven though marathon pace work is already prescribed in the Speed, extending it to long runs right after an Achilles twinge isn't worth the risk this close to race day -- that's a shoe rotation preference I should capture as a settings proposal rather than a plan change. For the rest of the week I'm mapping out Thursday's easy 6 in the Ghost, Friday rest, and Saturday's easy 5, also in the Ghost.\\n\\nFor Sunday's 18-miler with 4 at marathon pace, the prescribed plan already calls for Ghost 16 throughout, including the MP segment -- swapping shoes mid-run for just the pace block feels impractical, so I'm weighing whether to keep it simple and leave the whole run in the Ghost.\\n\\nGiven there's an Achilles twinge today, I think it's wiser not to change multiple variables at once -- I'll keep short MP touches in the Speed as already planned, but leave the long run in Ghost 16 while we monitor the Achilles.\\n\\nOnce Sunday's long run is complete, I can revisit shoe choice for W43's peak long run and race day decisions based on how the Achilles responds.\\n\\nFirst, I want to acknowledge the attached easy 9-miler — very clean execution, HR drifting only 6 bpm over 9 miles, steady pace, fully in Z2. But I'm noticing a discrepancy: Wednesday was scheduled as the MP tempo (8 mi with 5 at MP), yet the athlete logged a 9-mile easy run instead. I should flag this swap and ask about it, since the attachment doesn't specify which shoe they wore.\\n\\nChecking the prescribed week packet, I see the swap was already applied: Wednesday was set as the 8-mile MP tempo and Thursday the easy recovery run. So the athlete running easy on Wednesday instead is actually a deviation from the plan that already accounted for the swap - maybe they decided on their own to shift things again.\\n\\nI think the right response is to acknowledge the easy run as clean execution, not dwell on the missed tempo but ask what they're planning for the quality session, and address the Achilles twinge and shoe request.\\n\\nI need to compliment the clean easy 9, flag the Achilles twinge as something to monitor without over-medicalizing it, and figure out where the missed MP tempo should go given the Thursday work dinner conflict. I'm thinking through whether to slot MP into Thursday morning or shift it elsewhere, while also pushing back thoughtfully on the shoe request before patching the schedule.\\n\\nOh, I see - they can't run Thursday morning specifically because of the dinner, and asked to swap to Friday instead. The coach had already suggested keeping Thursday easy and flexible, but the athlete ran easy Wednesday rather than MP. So I'll propose keeping Thursday as prescribed easy, skipping the extra MP tempo, and letting Sunday's 18-miler with 4 MP serve as the week's key workout.\\n\\nOn the shoe preference, I'll gently flag concerns about using Speed for long runs without a hard no, suggesting they revisit after Sunday's run - that's a pending memory update, not urgent to resolve now. MP work in Speed is already fine as planned. For the Achilles twinge, this stays at a caution level: brief, resolved, keep monitoring each morning, no diagnosis or treatment advice, just a note to see a clinician if it recurs or worsens. I'm now drafting the reply structure, opening with specific feedback on the attached run data.\\n\\nActually, mid-run shoe swaps are messy — simpler to keep the whole long run in Ghost for now and revisit race-day shoe choice closer to taper, meaning no patch is needed there. Let me also reconsider Thursday given the athlete's work dinner that evening.\\n\\nNo, Sunday stays with Ghost 16 since I'm declining the shoe switch — I'll just confirm that verbally rather than patch anything. I do want to flag the shoe preference as a memory note though: athlete prefers Endorphin Speed 4 for long runs/MP work, but I'm holding Ghost through W43 given the Achilles history, revisiting after that long run. And I still need to work in the safety callout about the Achilles twinge.\\n\\nGiven the recent Achilles scare, I'll flag this as caution-level rather than urgent since it settled quickly — recommend the morning check and seeing a clinician if it worsens. Now let me pull the key numbers from the workout: distance roughly 9.15 miles, duration 1h23m12s, and I'm working out the average pace per kilometer.\\n\\nConfirming the pace calculation puts splits around 5:40/km with heart rate staying in Zone 2 (avg 148, max 154) and 60m of elevation gain across three consistent splits.\\n\\nRemaining splits stayed tight around 9:06/mi with HR drifting modestly from 147 to 153 bpm over the full run, and the final mile even picked up slightly to 8:58/mi while HR ticked up to 151-153. Overall this reads as clean, textbook easy aerobic running with minimal cardiac drift.\\n\\nWait, I notice this was logged as \\"Medium-long 9\\" with the Easy Run type and consistent Z2 pacing throughout — there's no marathon-pace tempo segment here, which means the athlete didn't do the MP tempo work we'd discussed. I should gently acknowledge that shift rather than assume, and think about when to slot in an MP effort later this week given the schedule — Thursday's uncertain, Saturday's a shakeout, and Sunday's long run already has 4 MP miles built in.\\n\\nI'll frame Sunday's 18-miler with 4 MP as the real race-rehearsal session, keeping Thursday easy. Now I'm drafting the settings proposal bullets for the dossier — noting the athlete's shoe preferences (Endorphin Speed 4 for long runs and MP work) alongside my coaching recommendation to stick with the Ghost 16 for long runs through the W43 peak given the Achilles history, keeping Speed shoes for MP work, and revisiting the race-day shoe decision after that peak long run. I want these bullets concise and focused on the actual ask for memory updates.\\n\\nFor the response body, I'm going with a practical, warm tone: praising the clean Z2 execution (HR 147→153 over 9 miles, well under the drift threshold, steady 9:05-9:07 pace with natural pickups), framing this as exactly the right recovery day after a 20-miler, then moving to address the Achilles twinge at mile 7 — acknowledging it settled quickly and isn't a red flag.\\n\\nThat said, I want to note it still warrants tomorrow's morning check protocol before running, and flag that same-day reporting is needed if it recurs on Thursday or during Sunday's MP block. I also want to gently flag that today was slated for the MP tempo swap but instead came out as a straight easy run — understandable given post-20 fatigue, but worth naming so we can reset the plan.\\n\\nThis means the MP tempo isn't happening this week; I'd rather not cram it into Thursday or stack quality close to Sunday, so Sunday's 18-with-4-at-MP becomes the week's sole race rehearsal, which is plenty since this is a build week, not peak. I'll offer the option of a small 2-mile MP touch inside Thursday's easy run if they want it, but my preference is to keep Thursday truly easy. On the shoe question about running both long runs and MP work in the Endorphin Speed 4 for the rest of the block, I'm acknowledging their preference before weighing in.\\n\\nand only revisit the carbon plate question once we see how the Achilles responds. Race shoe decision can wait until after W43 too — there's no rush. I want to flag this is their call to override if it feels off, but my inclination is to protect this one weekend given the twinge. Everything else stays as planned: easy Thursday, rest/travel Friday, shakeout Saturday, long run Sunday with the MP fueling dress rehearsal.\\n\\nI should also draft a safety callout flagging the Achilles twinge, with clear escalation criteria for a sports-med clinician if symptoms worsen, while coaching stays conservative in the meantime.\\n\\nFor the shoe proposal: the athlete prefers the Speed 4 for long runs and marathon-pace work, but given the pending Achilles check, I'll recommend keeping long runs in the Ghost through W43, letting MP work stay in the Speed as prescribed, and revisiting the full shoe plan after Sunday's long run.\\n\\nChecking the remaining prescribed days, most stay unchanged — Thursday's easy 6, Friday's rest, Saturday's shakeout — with Sunday's long 18 with 4 at MP being the key session to watch.\\n\\nSince the plan already has Sunday in the Ghost and nothing is actually changing, I don't think I need to patch anything — confirming the decision clearly in the message should be enough.\\n\\nI'm also second-guessing whether Wednesday's tempo should be touched, since it falls right on today's date. Given that past days stay stable by default and patches to them aren't typically allowed, I'll treat Wednesday as settled and leave it alone.\\n\\nI'll keep the response thorough but concise so it's easy for the athlete to digest.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MhKAj9NXGQZ3SBEpuo4rwg","name":"submit_mid_week_chat_reply","input":{"body":"Nice run — honest Z2 the whole way. HR climbed 147 → 153 across 9 miles (that's +6 bpm end-to-end, well inside the ≤10 target), pace locked between 9:05 and 9:07 with slight pickups to 8:58 in miles 3 and 9 as the legs loosened. Max HR only touched 154. Three days off a 20, that's the clean aerobic flush we wanted mid-week.\\n\\nOn the Achilles twinge at mile 7: thanks for flagging it. A couple of minutes of \\"noticeable\\" that settled and ran out by the end, on tired legs late in a 9-miler, is in a very different ballpark from September — I'm not alarmed. I'm also not shrugging. Any Achilles noise still earns the full morning check tomorrow (stairs, single-leg calf raises, stiffness scan) before you head out. If it shows up again on Thursday's easy miles, or during Sunday's MP block, tell me same day. See the callout below for the lines where you escalate to your sports-med clinician.\\n\\nOne honest thing to acknowledge: today's slot was the swapped-forward MP tempo, and the data says you ran a straight easy medium-long instead. No drama if that was a legs-driven call after Sunday's 20 — frankly, with how heavy Monday was, that's defensible. But it means the MP tempo is off the board for this week:\\n\\n- I don't want to shoehorn it into Thursday with the work dinner that night.\\n- I don't want to double up quality close to Sunday.\\n- **Sunday's 18 with the last 4 at MP becomes the sole race rehearsal this week.** That's enough — this isn't peak week, it's the build before peak.\\n\\nIf you *want* a short MP touch in Thursday's easy run (something like 2 mi continuous at 8:00–8:05 inside a 6-mile easy), say so and I'll adjust. My strong preference is Thursday stays truly easy and we land Sunday fresh.\\n\\nOn the shoe request — Endorphin Speed 4 for all long runs and MP work for the rest of the block:\\n\\nMP work in the Speed is already the plan and I'm good with that. Where I want to pump the brakes is **long runs in a carbon-plated shoe four weeks from the race, with an Achilles that twinged today.** The plate changes calf and Achilles loading, and the longer the run, the more cumulative it gets. We don't want to discover mid-20-miler that the shoe doesn't love your tendon.\\n\\nHere's what I'd like to do:\\n\\n- **Sunday's 18 (14 easy + 4 MP) stays in Ghost 16.** One shoe, one surface — a clean read on the MP finish without a new variable.\\n- **W43 peak long run (20 w/ 5 MP): we decide together after Sunday.** If this weekend is clean and the Achilles stays quiet all week, we have a real conversation about the MP portion in Speeds.\\n- **Race-day shoe: we lock after W43.** You've got time.\\n\\nIf that feels wrong, push back — this is a preference you're allowed to drive. But I'd rather hold the line for one more weekend given this morning's note.\\n\\nRest of the week stays as written: Thursday easy 6 in Ghost (4–5 is fine if the dinner pre-crunches you), Friday rest, Saturday 5 shakeout in Ghost, Sunday 18 w/ 4 MP in Ghost. Fueling on Sunday is the full dress rehearsal — same gels, same cadence, same bottle you plan to race with. Report back Sunday and we'll calibrate W43.","safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Achilles twinge during today's run — monitor and escalate if it changes","severity":"caution","body":"A brief Achilles note at mile 7 that settled is worth taking seriously given your history, even if it was milder than September. Keep the morning check (stairs + single-leg calf raises + stiffness scan) as the go/no-go for every run from here to race day. Escalate to your sports-med clinician or physio — not me — if any of these show up: pain that worsens through a run instead of settling, stiffness that's worse the next morning, a limp or gait change, visible swelling or a lump on the tendon, or anything that feels like a pop. I'll keep training conservative in the meantime."}],"settingsProposalBullets":["Athlete preference: use Endorphin Speed 4 for both long runs and all marathon-pace work for the remainder of this block (Ghost 16 currently prescribed for long runs).","Coach position pending Sunday's long run: hold long runs in Ghost 16 through W43 given today's Achilles twinge; MP work stays in Speed as currently prescribed; revisit long-run and race-day shoe choice after W43 long run."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30023,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":12352,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10669}},"diagnostics":null}	200	182810	tool_use	30023	12352	0	0	ok	\N	10669
