5c020889-40bf-4ecb-8a67-3a92c6e840d3	{"days": [{"date": "2026-08-31", "notes": "Travel day — full rest.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "~9:40/mi, HR ≤150", "distanceM": 8047, "structure": "5 mi conversational Z2. Shake out Sunday's long run."}, "date": "2026-09-01", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "Z2, HR ≤150", "distanceM": 11265, "structure": "7 mi steady aerobic, finish with 4×20s relaxed-fast strides on flat."}, "date": "2026-09-02", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "quality", "shoes": "Saucony Endorphin Speed 4", "paceOrHr": "MP block ~8:00–8:15/mi, HR upper Z3 (≤164)", "distanceM": 12875, "structure": "8 mi tempo: 2 mi easy WU → 4 mi continuous at marathon-pace effort (~8:00–8:15/mi, cap HR 164) → 2 mi easy CD. HR is the governor — if you need Z4 to hold pace, slow down."}, "date": "2026-09-03", "notes": "Rotation: tempo/MP this week. Hills return next Thursday.", "dayType": "quality"}, {"date": "2026-09-04", "notes": "Travel day — full rest.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "~9:50/mi, HR ≤148", "distanceM": 8047, "structure": "5 mi truly easy — pre-long shakeout. Z2 only."}, "date": "2026-09-05", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "long", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "HR ≤148 avg; pace is the output", "distanceM": 25750, "structure": "16 mi long run by HR. Cap average HR at 148 (top of Z2). If HR drifts into Z3 before mile 10, back off 15–20 sec/mi. Optional: last 2 mi comfortably strong (upper Z2 / low Z3) only if HR allows. Practice fueling: gel at mile 5 and mile 10, fluids every ~15 min with electrolytes."}, "date": "2026-09-06", "notes": "Longest run of the block. Fueling is part of the session — see notes above.", "dayType": "long"}], "week": "2026-W36"}	## Headline\nClean step-back week — 33.7 mi, 81% easy, long run at 10.8 with no late fade, and you came out of it feeling the best you have in a month. That's exactly what a down week is supposed to do. We're 11 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week we build back up: ~40 mi, a proper marathon-pace workout on Thursday (per the Thursday rotation), and the long run stretches to 16.\n\n## Concerns / flags\n- No body complaints, sleep bumped to 7.4 hr, stress down — all green lights to push forward.\n- Thursday's 800s two weeks running have landed around 6:36–6:40/mi (5K effort). Fine as fitness proof, but for marathon work the money is in sustained tempo/MP volume. This week we swap in tempo — it will feel less flashy and more useful.\n- Long-run drift was +8.5 bpm on Sunday with a Z3 tail (21% Z3). You held HR cap at 148 avg, which is what we asked. In this heat that drift is heat tax, not fitness. Keep running long by HR.\n- Shin-splint history: 40 mi is the biggest week of the block. The ramp from 33.7 → ~40 is about +18%, which is bigger than I'd normally like. I'm comfortable because last week was a true step-back, you're well-recovered, and we don't exceed last block's peak of 42.5. If anything twinges early in the week, tell me and we trim Sunday.\n\n## Your question — fueling the long run\nShort version: start fueling now, don't wait until the race to figure it out. Rough targets for runs ≥90 min:\n\n- **Before**: 40–60 g carbs 1–2 hr out (bagel + banana + honey, or oatmeal). 400–500 ml fluid.\n- **During**: 30–60 g carbs per hour after the first 45 min — one gel every 30–35 min is the simplest pattern. Sip fluid every ~15 min; in this heat add electrolytes (tab in a handheld, or a sports drink).\n- **Practice**: use the exact gels/drink you plan to use on race day. The gut trains like the legs do — the long run is where you build it. Expect some trial and error for the first 2–3 weeks.\n- **After**: carbs + protein within ~30 min (even just chocolate milk works).\n\nFor Sunday's 16: aim for a gel at ~mile 5 and ~mile 10, plus fluids. If you've been going without, start conservative at 30 g/hr and work up.\n\n## This week — the "why"\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's long.\n- **Wed easy 7 + strides**: aerobic anchor, strides to keep legs sharp before Thursday.\n- **Thu tempo (8 mi total)**: 2 mi WU → 4 mi at MP effort (~8:00–8:15/mi, HR upper Z3 ≤164) → 2 mi CD. First real block of marathon-pace volume. If HR is pinned at Z4 to hold pace, back off — the HR is the governor, not the watch.\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long shakeout, properly easy.\n- **Sun long 16 by HR**: cap avg HR ≤148. Pace will fall where it falls. If you want a nudge at the end, finish last 2 mi comfortably strong — only if HR allows.	\N	2026-08-30 20:00:41.950137+00	2026-08-30 20:00:41.950137+00	\N
