and your tempo splits (7:45–7:52) show real fitness. We're 14 weeks out from Lakeshore. This week I want to consolidate rather than push the mileage dial again, start introducing marathon-pace feel on the long run, and respect the heat.\n\n## Concerns / flags\n- **Relative effort jumped +33% over your 3-week average.** That's the kind of spike that, repeated, is how shin issues creep back in. One week like that is fine; two in a row isn't. So W33 holds mileage flat and keeps quality controlled.\n- **Long-run drift was +7.4 bpm** (144 → 151) and you flagged 25°C at 6 a.m. That's heat tax, not a fitness problem — but it means pace targets on the long run should be by effort/HR, not the watch.\n- **Thursday tempo structure was 3 fast miles sandwiched by easy.** Great session. Keep that template; we'll alternate hills and tempo weekly.\n\n## Your question — is 3:30 realistic?\nHonest answer: it's a stretch but a reasonable one. 3:30 is 8:00/mi. Right now your easy pace is 9:45 at mid-Z2 and you ran 7:45–7:52 for 3 tempo miles — that's a fitness level that typically supports something in the 3:35–3:45 range today. You have 14 weeks, a sensible 5-day structure, and you're ramping carefully. If the next 6 weeks of base + strength work land cleanly and we see your long-run cruise pace drift under 9:20 at the same HR, 3:30 is on the table. If it doesn't, we aim 3:35 and run smart. We'll know by late September. Either way, the training looks the same for now.\n\n## This week — the "why"\n- **Hold mileage ~34 mi** (slight pullback from 35.8) to absorb last week's load.\n- **Thursday = hill reps** on your Thursday hilly route — strength without the systemic cost of another tempo so soon.\n- **Sunday long run = 13 mi with last 3 at marathon-pace effort (~8:00–8:10/mi, cap HR at upper Z3).** First taste of goal-pace fatigue. If it's hot, run by effort and skip the MP miles — tell me after.\n- Easy days properly easy: HR under 150, pace will take care of itself.\n- Try to get both strength sessions in this week since you're not travelling.	{"Add Thursday rotation: hills one week, tempo/MP the next","Track long-run cruise pace at HR 148 as the 3:30 progress marker","Revisit goal pace realism in late September"}	2026-08-09 20:00:42.633121+00	2026-08-09 20:00:42.633121+00	[{"body": "You flagged 25°C at 6 a.m. last Sunday. Start earlier if you can, carry fluids, and if you feel dizzy, stop sweating, or get a headache that doesn't ease with water, stop and seek medical help. Running by effort/HR (not pace) in heat is the right call.", "title": "Heat on long runs", "severity": "info"}]
